// Generated by scripts/build_data.py from content/shorts. Do not edit by hand.
window.GENZ_CH={"1": {"en": "Arjuna sees his own family on the other side of the battlefield and completely breaks down. Full anxiety spiral. The whole Gita starts here.", "hi": "Arjun battlefield pe saamne apni hi family dekhta hai aur poora toot jaata hai. Full anxiety mode. Poori Gita yahin se shuru hoti hai."}, "2": {"en": "Krishna's crash course: you're more than your body, do the work without obsessing over results, keep your mind steady. Read one chapter? Read this.", "hi": "Krishna ka crash course: tum sirf body nahi ho, result ki tension chhodo, mind steady rakho. Ek chapter padhna hai toh ye padho."}, "3": {"en": "Running from responsibility isn't peace. Do your part, do it for something bigger than yourself, and don't make it all about you.", "hi": "Zimmedari se bhaagna peace nahi hai. Apna part karo, kisi badi cheez ke liye, aur sab apne baare mein mat banao."}, "4": {"en": "This wisdom is ancient, and Krishna returns whenever the world needs a reset. Work without ego and let wisdom burn away your past.", "hi": "Ye gyaan purana hai, aur jab duniya ko reset chahiye Krishna aate hain. Bina ego kaam karo, gyaan purane karma jala deta hai."}, "5": {"en": "Quitting versus doing? Doing your work without attachment wins. Find joy inside and outside pleasures lose their grip.", "hi": "Chhodna ya karna? Bina attachment kaam karna jeet-ta hai. Andar khushi dhoondo, bahar ke maze pakad kho dete hain."}, "6": {"en": "The meditation chapter. Your mind can be your best friend or worst enemy. Balance, practice and patience train it.", "hi": "Meditation wala chapter. Mind tumhara best friend bhi hai aur worst enemy bhi. Balance, practice aur sabr se train hota hai."}, "7": {"en": "Krishna is the thread running through everything: the taste of water, the light of the sun. Look closer and you'll see him everywhere.", "hi": "Krishna har cheez mein piroya dhaaga hain: paani ka swaad, suraj ki roshni. Dhyaan se dekho, har jagah dikhenge."}, "8": {"en": "What you think about most is where you end up. Remember the divine always, even at the very end.", "hi": "Jo sabse zyada sochte ho, wahin pahunchte ho. Divine ko hamesha yaad rakho, aakhri pal mein bhi."}, "9": {"en": "The royal secret: a leaf, a flower or some water offered with love is enough. Turn your whole life into an offering.", "hi": "Raja raaz: pyaar se diya ek patta, phool ya paani kaafi hai. Poori life ko offering bana do."}, "10": {"en": "Wherever you see brilliance, beauty or power, that's a spark of the divine. Krishna lists his best appearances.", "hi": "Jahan bhi talent, sundarta ya taakat dikhe, woh divine ki chingari hai. Krishna apne best roop ginate hain."}, "11": {"en": "The big reveal. Arjuna sees Krishna's cosmic form, as bright as a thousand suns, and learns he's just the instrument.", "hi": "Sabse bada reveal. Arjun Krishna ka vishwaroop dekhta hai, hazaar suraj jitna tez, aur samajhta hai woh bas nimitt hai."}, "12": {"en": "The love chapter. Can't focus? Practise. Can't practise? Serve. Can't serve? Let go of results. There's a path for everyone.", "hi": "Pyaar wala chapter. Focus nahi hota? Practice karo. Woh nahi? Seva karo. Woh bhi nahi? Result chhodo. Sabke liye raasta hai."}, "13": {"en": "Your body is the field, your soul is the knower. Learn the difference and you see the same divine in everyone.", "hi": "Tumhara body khet hai, aatma jaanne wali. Farak samjho toh sab mein ek hi divine dikhta hai."}, "14": {"en": "Three energies run your moods: clarity, hustle and laziness. Notice which is in charge, then rise above all three.", "hi": "Teen energies tumhara mood chalati hain: clarity, hustle aur aalas. Dekho kaun in charge hai, phir teeno se upar utho."}, "15": {"en": "Life is an upside-down tree rooted in the divine. Cut through attachment and find the Supreme Person beyond it all.", "hi": "Zindagi divine mein jadi ulta ped hai. Attachment kaato aur sabse pare Purushottam ko dhoondo."}, "16": {"en": "Green flags versus red flags of the soul. Lust, anger and greed are the three exits to avoid.", "hi": "Aatma ke green flags versus red flags. Vaasna, gussa aur laalach, teen exits jinse bachna hai."}, "17": {"en": "You are what you believe. Food, discipline and giving each come in pure, hyped and lazy versions.", "hi": "Tum wahi ho jis pe bharosa karte ho. Khaana, tap aur daan, sab shuddh, hyped aur aalsi version mein aate hain."}, "18": {"en": "The finale. Do your own work, let go of results, trust the divine completely. Arjuna's confusion is gone. Glow-up complete.", "hi": "Finale. Apna kaam karo, result chhodo, divine pe poora bharosa rakho. Arjun ka confusion gaya. Glow-up complete."}};
window.GENZ={"1.1": {"en": "Blind King Dhritarashtra asks: \"What's happening on the battlefield?\" The whole Gita is the answer to this one anxious question.", "hi": "Andhe raja Dhritarashtra poochte hain: \"Battlefield pe kya ho raha hai?\" Poori Gita isi ek anxious sawaal ka jawaab hai."}, "1.2": {"en": "Duryodhana sees the other army lined up and runs straight to his teacher. Nervous energy, trying to look confident.", "hi": "Duryodhan saamne ki army dekhta hai aur seedha guru ke paas bhaagta hai. Andar se nervous, bahar se confident."}, "1.3": {"en": "\"Look, teacher, your own student is leading their army.\" Duryodhana throwing subtle shade at Drona.", "hi": "\"Dekhiye guruji, aapka hi student unki army lead kar raha hai.\" Duryodhan ka Drona pe halka sa taunt."}, "1.4": {"en": "Duryodhana lists the legends on the other side: Bhima, Arjuna, and big names. He's lowkey scared.", "hi": "Duryodhan saamne ke legends gin raha hai: Bheem, Arjun aur bade naam. Andar se thoda darra hua hai."}, "1.5": {"en": "More heavy hitters on the Pandava side. Duryodhana keeps counting threats instead of trusting his own team.", "hi": "Pandavon ki taraf aur bhi heavy hitters. Duryodhan apni team pe bharosa karne ki jagah threats gin raha hai."}, "1.6": {"en": "Young warriors too, including Abhimanyu and Draupadi's sons. Every name makes Duryodhana more anxious.", "hi": "Young warriors bhi hain, Abhimanyu aur Draupadi ke bete. Har naam ke saath Duryodhan ki tension badh rahi hai."}, "1.7": {"en": "Now he hypes his own side: \"Let me remind you of our commanders.\" Classic pep talk to calm himself down.", "hi": "Ab apni side ko hype karta hai: \"Apne commanders yaad dila doon.\" Khud ko shaant karne wala pep talk."}, "1.8": {"en": "Drona, Bhishma, Karna and more. Duryodhana flexing his roster like a fantasy team.", "hi": "Drona, Bheeshma, Karna aur bhi. Duryodhan apni team aise flex kar raha hai jaise fantasy league ho."}, "1.9": {"en": "\"So many heroes ready to die for me.\" When your confidence depends on others, it's shaky.", "hi": "\"Kitne heroes mere liye jaan dene ko taiyaar hain.\" Jab confidence dusron pe tika ho, toh woh kamzor hota hai."}, "1.10": {"en": "\"Our army feels weak, theirs feels strong.\" Comparing yourself to others always messes with your head.", "hi": "\"Hamari army kamzor lagti hai, unki strong.\" Dusron se compare karna hamesha dimaag kharab karta hai."}, "1.11": {"en": "\"Everyone, protect Bhishma at all costs!\" Duryodhana's whole plan rests on one person. Risky strategy.", "hi": "\"Sab log Bheeshma ko har haal mein bachao!\" Poora plan ek insaan pe tika hai. Risky strategy."}, "1.12": {"en": "Bhishma roars and blows his conch to boost Duryodhana's mood. The grandpa hype man moment.", "hi": "Bheeshma sher ki tarah garajte hain aur shankh bajate hain taaki Duryodhan ka mood bane. Dada ji ka hype moment."}, "1.13": {"en": "Conches, drums, horns all at once. The noise is insane. Battle soundtrack: on.", "hi": "Shankh, dhol, nagade, sab ek saath. Shor zabardast. Battle ka soundtrack: on."}, "1.14": {"en": "Krishna and Arjuna, on a chariot with white horses, blow their divine conches. Main characters have entered.", "hi": "Safed ghodon wale rath pe Krishna aur Arjun apne divya shankh bajate hain. Main characters ki entry."}, "1.15": {"en": "Every hero has a named conch, like a signature sound. Krishna's is Panchajanya. Iconic.", "hi": "Har hero ke shankh ka naam hai, jaise signature sound. Krishna ka Panchajanya. Iconic."}, "1.16": {"en": "Yudhishthira, Nakula and Sahadeva join in. The Pandava brothers are fully in sync.", "hi": "Yudhishthir, Nakul aur Sahadev bhi shamil. Pandav bhai poore sync mein hain."}, "1.17": {"en": "More warriors answer the call. The Pandava side is loud, united and ready.", "hi": "Aur warriors bhi jawaab dete hain. Pandav side loud, united aur ready hai."}, "1.18": {"en": "Everyone blows their conch again and again. It's a full squad roll call.", "hi": "Sab baar-baar shankh bajate hain. Poore squad ka roll call."}, "1.19": {"en": "The sound shakes earth and sky, and the Kauravas feel it in their hearts. Unity is loud.", "hi": "Awaaz dharti-aasmaan hila deti hai, aur Kauravon ke dil kaanp jaate hain. Unity ki awaaz tez hoti hai."}, "1.20": {"en": "Arjuna, Hanuman on his flag, picks up his bow. The fight is about to begin.", "hi": "Arjun, jiske jhande pe Hanuman hain, dhanush uthata hai. Ladai shuru hone wali hai."}, "1.21": {"en": "Arjuna: \"Krishna, take my chariot to the middle.\" He wants a clear look before the battle.", "hi": "Arjun: \"Krishna, mera rath beech mein le chalo.\" Ladai se pehle saaf dekhna chahta hai."}, "1.22": {"en": "\"Let me see who I'm actually up against.\" Smart move. Know what you're facing.", "hi": "\"Dekhne do main kis se lad raha hoon.\" Smart move. Pehle samjho kis cheez ka saamna hai."}, "1.23": {"en": "Arjuna wants to see who showed up to support Duryodhana's bad choices.", "hi": "Arjun dekhna chahta hai ki Duryodhan ke galat decisions ko support karne kaun aaya hai."}, "1.24": {"en": "Krishna parks the chariot right in front of Bhishma and Drona and says: \"Look at them.\" Plot twist loading.", "hi": "Krishna rath ko Bheeshma aur Drona ke saamne rokte hain aur kehte hain: \"Dekho inhe.\" Plot twist loading."}, "1.25": {"en": "Krishna's \"look at them\" is deliberate. He knows exactly what Arjuna is about to feel.", "hi": "Krishna ka \"dekho inhe\" soch-samajh ke hai. Unhe pata hai Arjun ab kya feel karega."}, "1.26": {"en": "Arjuna sees grandfathers, teachers, cousins, friends. The enemy is literally family.", "hi": "Arjun dekhta hai dada, guru, cousins, dost. Dushman toh apni hi family hai."}, "1.27": {"en": "In-laws and close friends on both sides. Suddenly this isn't a war. It's a family breakup.", "hi": "Dono taraf sasural wale aur dost. Achanak ye war nahi, family breakup lagne laga."}, "1.28": {"en": "Arjuna gets hit by a wave of emotion and starts to break down.", "hi": "Arjun pe emotions ki lehar aati hai aur woh tootne lagta hai."}, "1.29": {"en": "Legs weak, mouth dry, body shaking, goosebumps. That's a full panic attack, described thousands of years ago.", "hi": "Pair kamzor, munh sookha, body kaanp rahi, rongte khade. Ye poora panic attack hai, hazaaron saal pehle likha hua."}, "1.30": {"en": "His bow slips, his skin burns, his head spins. Even the greatest warrior can hit a wall.", "hi": "Dhanush phisal raha, skin jal rahi, sar ghoom raha. Sabse bada warrior bhi deewar se takra sakta hai."}, "1.31": {"en": "\"I only see bad signs. Nothing good comes from killing my own people.\"", "hi": "\"Mujhe sirf bure sign dikh rahe hain. Apno ko maar ke kuch achha nahi hoga.\""}, "1.32": {"en": "\"I don't want the win, the throne or the luxury. What's the point of any of it?\" Total burnout energy.", "hi": "\"Mujhe jeet, raaj ya luxury kuch nahi chahiye. Iska point kya hai?\" Total burnout energy."}, "1.33": {"en": "\"The people I'd want to share the success with are the ones standing here to fight.\"", "hi": "\"Jinke saath success share karni thi, wahi log yahan ladne khade hain.\""}, "1.34": {"en": "Teachers, fathers, sons, uncles, in-laws: Arjuna sees them all as his own people. That's the pain.", "hi": "Guru, pita, bete, chacha, sasural wale: Arjun ko sab apne lagte hain. Dard yahi hai."}, "1.35": {"en": "\"Even for all three worlds I wouldn't kill them, let alone for this earth.\"", "hi": "\"Teenon lok mil jaayein tab bhi inhe nahi maarunga, yeh dharti toh kya cheez hai.\""}, "1.36": {"en": "\"Even if they're wrong, what joy is there in destroying them? It'll only leave guilt.\"", "hi": "\"Galat hain toh bhi, inhe khatam karke kya khushi milegi? Sirf guilt bachega.\""}, "1.37": {"en": "\"How could we ever be happy after killing our own family?\" Arjuna's heart is overruling everything.", "hi": "\"Apni family ko maar ke hum kaise khush rahenge?\" Arjun ka dil sab pe haavi hai."}, "1.38": {"en": "\"They're blinded by greed and don't see the damage. But we can see it.\"", "hi": "\"Woh greed mein andhe hain, nuksaan nahi dekh rahe. Par hum toh dekh sakte hain.\""}, "1.39": {"en": "\"If we know this is wrong, why shouldn't we walk away?\" Arjuna building his case to quit.", "hi": "\"Jab pata hai ye galat hai, toh hum peeche kyun na hatein?\" Arjun quit karne ka case bana raha hai."}, "1.40": {"en": "\"When families fall apart, traditions and values go with them, and chaos follows.\"", "hi": "\"Jab family toot-ti hai, toh values aur traditions bhi chale jaate hain, aur chaos aa jaata hai.\""}, "1.41": {"en": "Arjuna worries society will lose its moral compass if this war happens. Big-picture fear.", "hi": "Arjun ko darr hai ki is war se society ka moral compass kho jaayega. Big-picture darr."}, "1.42": {"en": "He fears the damage will hit generations, even the ancestors. His anxiety is now going full worst-case.", "hi": "Usse lagta hai nuksaan peedhiyon tak jaayega, purvajon tak bhi. Anxiety ab worst-case mode mein hai."}, "1.43": {"en": "\"Those who break families destroy traditions that took ages to build.\"", "hi": "\"Jo family todte hain, woh sadiyon ki traditions khatam kar dete hain.\""}, "1.44": {"en": "\"We've heard that people who destroy family values suffer badly.\" Fear is doing the talking now.", "hi": "\"Suna hai jo family values todte hain, woh bura bhugatte hain.\" Ab darr bol raha hai."}, "1.45": {"en": "\"We're about to do something terrible just for power and comfort.\" Guilt hits hard.", "hi": "\"Sirf power aur aaram ke liye hum kuch bahut galat karne ja rahe hain.\" Guilt zor se lagta hai."}, "1.46": {"en": "\"I'd rather let them kill me, unarmed, than fight.\" Arjuna is ready to give up completely.", "hi": "\"Main bina hathiyar ke mar jaana pasand karunga, ladne se.\" Arjun poori tarah haar maanne ko taiyaar hai."}, "1.47": {"en": "Arjuna drops his bow, sits down, and breaks. Rock bottom. And this is exactly where the Gita begins.", "hi": "Arjun dhanush gira deta hai, baith jaata hai, toot jaata hai. Rock bottom. Aur Gita yahin se shuru hoti hai."}, "2.1": {"en": "Arjuna's crying, overwhelmed, frozen. Krishna sees it all and steps in. Big talk incoming.", "hi": "Arjun ro raha hai, overwhelmed hai, freeze ho gaya hai. Krishna sab dekh rahe hain. Ab badi baat hone wali hai."}, "2.2": {"en": "Krishna: \"Bro, why are you breaking down right now? This isn't you, and it won't get you anywhere.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Is time pe kyun toot rahe ho? Ye tum nahi ho, aur isse kuch nahi milega.\""}, "2.3": {"en": "This isn't you. Stop doom-spiralling, get up, and handle it. You're bigger than this moment.", "hi": "Ye tum nahi ho. Overthinking band karo, utho, aur handle karo. Tum is moment se bade ho."}, "2.4": {"en": "Arjuna: \"How do I fight people I literally look up to?\" Real dilemma, real pain.", "hi": "Arjun: \"Jinki main izzat karta hoon, unse kaise ladun?\" Real dilemma, real dard."}, "2.5": {"en": "Arjuna would rather be broke than hurt his teachers. Any win built on that feels toxic to him.", "hi": "Arjun ko apne gurus ko hurt karne se better bheekh maangna lagta hai. Aisi jeet usko toxic lagti hai."}, "2.6": {"en": "Arjuna doesn't even know what winning means anymore. Win or lose, someone he loves gets hurt.", "hi": "Arjun ko pata hi nahi jeet kya hai. Jeete ya haare, koi apna hi hurt hoga."}, "2.7": {"en": "Arjuna finally admits: \"I'm confused. I need help. Guide me.\" Asking for help is the first real step.", "hi": "Arjun finally maanta hai: \"Main confused hoon, guide karo.\" Help maangna hi pehla real step hai."}, "2.8": {"en": "Even owning the whole world wouldn't fix this pain. Money and power can't heal a confused mind.", "hi": "Poori duniya mil jaaye tab bhi ye dard nahi jaayega. Paisa aur power confused mind ko heal nahi karte."}, "2.9": {"en": "Arjuna says \"I won't fight\" and goes silent. Full shutdown mode.", "hi": "Arjun bolta hai \"Main nahi ladunga\" aur chup ho jaata hai. Full shutdown mode."}, "2.10": {"en": "Krishna smiles. Not mocking, just calm. He knows this crisis is where the growth starts.", "hi": "Krishna muskurate hain. Mazaak nahi, bas calm. Unhe pata hai growth yahin se shuru hoti hai."}, "2.11": {"en": "You're overthinking things that don't deserve your grief. Wise people don't spiral over life or death.", "hi": "Jis baat pe dukh nahi hona chahiye, uspe overthink kar rahe ho. Samajhdaar log zindagi-maut pe spiral nahi karte."}, "2.12": {"en": "You, me, everyone here: we always existed and always will. You're not as temporary as you think.", "hi": "Tum, main, sab: hum hamesha the aur hamesha rahenge. Tum utne temporary nahi ho jitna sochte ho."}, "2.13": {"en": "Childhood, teen years, old age, then a new body. You keep upgrading; the real you stays.", "hi": "Bachpan, jawani, budhapa, phir naya body. Tum upgrade hote rehte ho, asli tum wahi rehte ho."}, "2.14": {"en": "Feelings come and go like weather. One bad day isn't your whole story. Let it pass and keep going.", "hi": "Feelings mausam ki tarah aati-jaati hain. Ek bura din poori story nahi. Guzarne do, aage badho."}, "2.15": {"en": "Stay the same whether it's pain or pleasure. That steady person can't be shaken by anything.", "hi": "Dukh ho ya sukh, same raho. Aise insaan ko koi hila nahi sakta."}, "2.16": {"en": "What's fake never really exists. What's real never disappears. Learn to tell the difference.", "hi": "Jo fake hai woh kabhi tikta nahi. Jo real hai woh kabhi jaata nahi. Farak samjho."}, "2.17": {"en": "The thing that runs through everything can't be destroyed. Nobody can delete the real you.", "hi": "Jo sab mein hai, usko koi khatam nahi kar sakta. Asli tumhe koi delete nahi kar sakta."}, "2.18": {"en": "Bodies have an expiry date. The soul doesn't. So do what you have to do.", "hi": "Body ki expiry date hai, aatma ki nahi. Toh jo karna hai woh karo."}, "2.19": {"en": "Thinking the soul kills or gets killed? Both takes are wrong. It's untouchable.", "hi": "Aatma maarti hai ya marti hai? Dono galat. Woh untouchable hai."}, "2.20": {"en": "The real you was never born and can't die. Bodies change, but the one watching it all stays.", "hi": "Asli tum na kabhi paida hue, na maroge. Body badalti hai, par dekhne wala wahi rehta hai."}, "2.21": {"en": "Once you know the soul can't be destroyed, the whole fear of killing and dying changes.", "hi": "Jab samajh aa jaaye ki aatma amar hai, toh maarne-marne ka darr hi badal jaata hai."}, "2.22": {"en": "Changing bodies is like changing clothes. Old fit off, new fit on. Same you inside.", "hi": "Body badalna kapde badalne jaisa hai. Purana outfit off, naya on. Andar wahi tum."}, "2.23": {"en": "Weapons can't cut it, fire can't burn it, water can't wet it, wind can't dry it. Built different.", "hi": "Hathiyar kaat nahi sakte, aag jala nahi sakti, paani bhigo nahi sakta, hawa sukha nahi sakti. Built different."}, "2.24": {"en": "The soul can't be cut, burned, soaked or dried. It's everywhere, steady, and forever.", "hi": "Aatma na kat-ti, na jalti, na bheegti, na sookhti. Har jagah, steady aur hamesha."}, "2.25": {"en": "You can't see it or fully figure it out, and it never changes. So stop grieving.", "hi": "Na dikhti hai, na poori samajh aati hai, na badalti hai. Toh dukh band karo."}, "2.26": {"en": "Even if you think the soul dies every time, grieving still doesn't help. Stay strong.", "hi": "Agar maano ki aatma baar-baar marti hai, tab bhi rona kaam nahi aata. Strong raho."}, "2.27": {"en": "Whoever's born will die, and whoever dies comes back. Don't stress over what can't be avoided.", "hi": "Jo paida hua woh jaayega, jo gaya woh lautega. Jo tal nahi sakta uski tension kyun?"}, "2.28": {"en": "We come from the unknown and go back to it. We only see the middle part. Why panic?", "hi": "Unknown se aaye, unknown mein jaayenge. Hum sirf beech ka part dekhte hain. Panic kyun?"}, "2.29": {"en": "Some see the soul as a miracle, some talk about it, some hear about it. Few actually get it.", "hi": "Koi aatma ko miracle maanta hai, koi baat karta hai, koi sunta hai. Samajhte bahut kam hain."}, "2.30": {"en": "The soul in every body is eternal. Nobody is ever truly lost. Don't drown in grief.", "hi": "Har body ki aatma amar hai. Koi sach mein khota nahi. Dukh mein mat doobo."}, "2.31": {"en": "This is literally your role. Backing out of the right fight doesn't suit you.", "hi": "Ye tumhara role hai. Sahi ladai se peeche hatna tumhe suit nahi karta."}, "2.32": {"en": "A real chance to stand up for what's right is rare. Lucky are those who get one.", "hi": "Sahi cheez ke liye khade hone ka mauka rare hai. Lucky hain jinhe milta hai."}, "2.33": {"en": "Skip this fight and you lose your purpose, your respect, and your peace.", "hi": "Ye ladai chhodi toh purpose, respect aur sukoon, teeno jaayenge."}, "2.34": {"en": "Run away and people will talk about it forever. For someone respected, that hurts more than anything.", "hi": "Bhaage toh log hamesha baat karenge. Respected insaan ke liye ye sabse zyada chubhta hai."}, "2.35": {"en": "The legends will think you got scared. The ones who hyped you up will lose respect.", "hi": "Legends sochenge tum darr gaye. Jo tumhe hype karte the, woh respect kho denge."}, "2.36": {"en": "Haters will roast you nonstop. What's more painful than that?", "hi": "Haters nonstop roast karenge. Isse zyada dard kya hoga?"}, "2.37": {"en": "Lose and you still win something. Win and you get it all. So get up and fight.", "hi": "Haaro toh bhi kuch milega, jeeto toh sab kuch. Toh utho aur lado."}, "2.38": {"en": "Pleasure or pain, gain or loss, win or fail: treat them the same and just do your duty.", "hi": "Sukh-dukh, fayda-nuksaan, jeet-haar: sabko same dekho aur apna kaam karo."}, "2.39": {"en": "Theory done. Now the practical: how to work without getting trapped by your actions.", "hi": "Theory ho gayi. Ab practical: kaam karo bina usme phanse."}, "2.40": {"en": "On this path no effort is ever wasted. Even a little practice protects you from big fears.", "hi": "Is raaste pe koi effort waste nahi hota. Thodi si practice bhi bade darr se bachati hai."}, "2.41": {"en": "Focused mind = one clear goal. Scattered mind = a hundred tabs open and nothing done.", "hi": "Focused mind = ek clear goal. Scattered mind = sau tabs khule, kaam zero."}, "2.42": {"en": "Some people use religion just to chase rewards and luxury. That noise kills real focus.", "hi": "Kuch log dharm ko sirf rewards aur luxury ke liye use karte hain. Woh noise focus khatam karta hai."}, "2.43": {"en": "Chasing heaven, perks and power as the goal? Your mind stays scattered and never settles.", "hi": "Swarg, perks aur power ko hi goal banaoge toh mind kabhi settle nahi hoga."}, "2.44": {"en": "Hooked on pleasure and power? You'll never build the deep focus that actually matters.", "hi": "Pleasure aur power ke addict ho? Toh asli deep focus kabhi nahi banega."}, "2.45": {"en": "Rise above the push and pull of moods. Stop obsessing over getting and keeping stuff. Stay centered.", "hi": "Moods ke push-pull se upar utho. Cheezein paane aur bachane ki tension chhodo. Centered raho."}, "2.46": {"en": "When you've found the ocean, you don't need the well. Real wisdom covers everything the rituals promise.", "hi": "Samundar mil gaya toh kuan kya karna? Asli gyaan mein sab rituals ka fayda aa jaata hai."}, "2.47": {"en": "You control the effort, not the outcome. Grades, likes, promotions aren't your department. Do the work, drop the result anxiety.", "hi": "Effort tumhare haath mein hai, result nahi. Marks, likes, promotion tumhara department nahi. Kaam karo, result ki tension chhodo."}, "2.48": {"en": "Do your thing with a steady mind. Win or lose, stay balanced. That calm focus is real yoga.", "hi": "Apna kaam steady mind se karo. Jeet ho ya haar, balance mat khona. Yahi asli yoga hai."}, "2.49": {"en": "Working only for rewards keeps you stressed. Working with a calm mind keeps you free.", "hi": "Sirf reward ke liye kaam karoge toh stress rahega. Calm mind se karoge toh free rahoge."}, "2.50": {"en": "A balanced mind is the real skill. Yoga is basically being great at what you do, without stress.", "hi": "Balanced mind hi asli skill hai. Yoga matlab apne kaam mein best hona, bina stress ke."}, "2.51": {"en": "Wise people work hard but don't cling to the results. That's how they escape the endless cycle.", "hi": "Samajhdaar log mehnat karte hain par result se chipakte nahi. Isliye cycle se nikal jaate hain."}, "2.52": {"en": "Once you see through the confusion, all the hype and noise around you stops mattering.", "hi": "Jab confusion clear ho jaata hai, toh aas-paas ka hype aur noise matter nahi karta."}, "2.53": {"en": "When your mind stops getting pulled around by every opinion and stays steady, that's the real breakthrough.", "hi": "Jab har opinion se mind idhar-udhar nahi bhaagta aur steady rehta hai, wahi asli breakthrough hai."}, "2.54": {"en": "Arjuna asks: \"What does a truly steady person look like? How do they talk, sit, move?\"", "hi": "Arjun poochta hai: \"Sach mein steady insaan kaisa hota hai? Kaise bolta, baithta, chalta hai?\""}, "2.55": {"en": "When you stop needing outside stuff to be happy and feel complete inside, you're truly steady.", "hi": "Jab khush rehne ke liye bahar ki cheezein nahi chahiye aur andar se complete feel karo, tab tum steady ho."}, "2.56": {"en": "Not shaken by pain, not chasing pleasure, free from fear and anger. That's peak calm.", "hi": "Dukh se hilta nahi, sukh ke peeche bhaagta nahi, darr aur gusse se free. Peak calm."}, "2.57": {"en": "Good news or bad news, they don't overreact either way. That's real stability.", "hi": "Achhi news ho ya buri, overreact nahi karta. Yahi asli stability hai."}, "2.58": {"en": "Like a tortoise pulling in its limbs, pull your senses back from distractions. That's focus.", "hi": "Kachhua jaise apne pair andar kheench leta hai, waise senses ko distractions se wapas kheencho. Yahi focus hai."}, "2.59": {"en": "You can avoid temptations, but the craving stays. It only fades when you find something higher.", "hi": "Temptation se door reh sakte ho, par craving rehti hai. Woh tab jaati hai jab kuch bada mil jaaye."}, "2.60": {"en": "Your senses are strong enough to drag even a smart person off track. Stay alert.", "hi": "Senses itne strong hain ki smart insaan ko bhi track se hata dein. Alert raho."}, "2.61": {"en": "Control your senses and stay focused on the Divine. That's where steady wisdom comes from.", "hi": "Senses control karo aur Bhagwan pe focus rakho. Steady gyaan wahin se aata hai."}, "2.62": {"en": "Keep thinking about something and you get attached. Attachment becomes wanting. Blocked wanting becomes anger. Sound familiar?", "hi": "Kisi cheez ke baare mein baar-baar socho toh attachment hota hai, phir chahat, phir gussa. Relatable?"}, "2.63": {"en": "Anger fogs your head, you forget who you are, you make choices you regret. Catch the spiral early.", "hi": "Gusse mein dimaag dhundhla, tum bhool jaate ho tum kaun ho, phir galat decisions. Spiral jaldi pakdo."}, "2.64": {"en": "Enjoy the world without love-hate drama and with your senses in check. That's how you find peace.", "hi": "Duniya enjoy karo bina love-hate drama ke, senses control mein rakho. Wahi peace hai."}, "2.65": {"en": "With a peaceful mind all sadness fades, and your thinking gets clear fast.", "hi": "Peaceful mind mein saara dukh khatam ho jaata hai aur soch jaldi clear hoti hai."}, "2.66": {"en": "No focus, no peace. No peace, no real happiness. It all starts with a steady mind.", "hi": "Focus nahi toh peace nahi. Peace nahi toh asli khushi nahi. Sab steady mind se shuru hota hai."}, "2.67": {"en": "Let your senses run wild and they'll drag your mind like wind pushing a boat off course.", "hi": "Senses ko khula chhodo toh woh mind ko aise le jaate hain jaise hawa naav ko raaste se bhatka de."}, "2.68": {"en": "When your senses don't control you, your wisdom becomes rock solid.", "hi": "Jab senses tumhe control nahi karte, tab tumhara gyaan rock solid ho jaata hai."}, "2.69": {"en": "What the world hypes, the wise ignore. What the world ignores, the wise see clearly. Different vision.", "hi": "Duniya jisko hype karti hai, wise log ignore karte hain. Jo duniya ignore karti hai, woh unhe saaf dikhta hai."}, "2.70": {"en": "Rivers keep flowing in, but the ocean stays calm. Let desires come and go. That's peace.", "hi": "Nadiyaan girti rehti hain, par samundar calm rehta hai. Desires aane-jaane do. Yahi peace hai."}, "2.71": {"en": "Drop the cravings, the ego and the \"mine, mine, mine\" mindset. That's when you find real peace.", "hi": "Cravings, ego aur \"mera, mera\" wali soch chhodo. Tabhi asli sukoon milta hai."}, "2.72": {"en": "This is the ultimate state: total clarity and calm. Reach it, even at the very end, and you're free.", "hi": "Ye ultimate state hai: total clarity aur calm. Aakhri pal mein bhi mil jaaye toh tum free ho."}, "3.1": {"en": "Arjuna: \"If knowledge is better than action, why push me into this fight?\" Fair question.", "hi": "Arjun: \"Agar gyaan action se better hai, toh mujhe ladai mein kyun dhakel rahe ho?\" Fair sawaal."}, "3.2": {"en": "\"Your advice feels contradictory. Just give me one clear path.\" We've all wanted this.", "hi": "\"Aapki baatein confusing lag rahi hain. Bas ek clear raasta batao.\" Ye sabne kabhi chaha hai."}, "3.3": {"en": "Two paths: the path of knowledge for thinkers, the path of action for doers. Both are valid.", "hi": "Do raaste: sochne walon ke liye gyaan ka, karne walon ke liye karm ka. Dono valid hain."}, "3.4": {"en": "Just quitting work doesn't make you free. Escaping isn't the same as growing.", "hi": "Kaam chhod dene se freedom nahi milti. Bhaagna aur grow karna alag cheez hai."}, "3.5": {"en": "Nobody can do nothing, even for a second. Your nature keeps you moving. So move with purpose.", "hi": "Koi ek second bhi kuch na kare, ye possible nahi. Nature tumhe chalati rehti hai. Toh purpose ke saath chalo."}, "3.6": {"en": "Sitting still while your mind binges on cravings? That's just pretending. Fake discipline.", "hi": "Baahar se shaant baithe ho par mind cravings mein doob raha hai? Ye bas dikhawa hai. Fake discipline."}, "3.7": {"en": "Control your mind, then act without clinging to results. That person really stands out.", "hi": "Mind control karo, phir result se chipke bina kaam karo. Aisa insaan sach mein alag hota hai."}, "3.8": {"en": "Doing something beats doing nothing. Even staying alive takes action. Stop waiting for the perfect moment.", "hi": "Kuch na karne se kuch karna better hai. Zinda rehne ke liye bhi action chahiye. Perfect moment ka wait band karo."}, "3.9": {"en": "Work done only for yourself traps you. Work done as an offering sets you free.", "hi": "Sirf apne liye kiya kaam phansata hai. Offering ki tarah kiya kaam free karta hai."}, "3.10": {"en": "From the start, life was designed around giving. Give, and the universe gives back.", "hi": "Shuru se life giving pe based hai. Do, aur universe wapas deta hai."}, "3.11": {"en": "Support each other, and everyone wins. Life works best as a team sport.", "hi": "Ek dusre ko support karo, sab jeetenge. Life team sport ki tarah best chalti hai."}, "3.12": {"en": "Taking from the world without giving anything back? That's basically stealing.", "hi": "Duniya se lete raho aur kuch wapas na do? Ye basically chori hai."}, "3.13": {"en": "Share first, then enjoy. Living only for yourself leaves you empty.", "hi": "Pehle share karo, phir enjoy karo. Sirf apne liye jeena khaali kar deta hai."}, "3.14": {"en": "Food comes from rain, rain from nature's cycle, and that cycle runs on everyone's effort. It's all connected.", "hi": "Khaana baarish se, baarish nature ke cycle se, aur woh cycle sabke effort se chalta hai. Sab connected hai."}, "3.15": {"en": "Every action traces back to something bigger. The divine is present in every act of giving.", "hi": "Har action kisi badi cheez se juda hai. Har dene wale kaam mein divine maujood hai."}, "3.16": {"en": "Living just for your own pleasure, ignoring the cycle? That's a wasted life.", "hi": "Sirf apne maze ke liye jeena, cycle ko ignore karna? Ye zindagi waste karna hai."}, "3.17": {"en": "When you're truly at peace with yourself, you don't need anything to prove.", "hi": "Jab tum khud se sach mein khush ho, toh kuch prove karne ki zaroorat nahi rehti."}, "3.18": {"en": "Someone fully content has nothing to gain or lose from doing or not doing. Total freedom.", "hi": "Jo poori tarah santusht hai, use karne ya na karne se kuch milta-jaata nahi. Total freedom."}, "3.19": {"en": "So do what needs to be done, without attachment. That's the path to the highest.", "hi": "Toh jo karna zaroori hai woh karo, bina attachment ke. Yahi sabse upar ka raasta hai."}, "3.20": {"en": "King Janaka reached the top while working. And you set an example for others too.", "hi": "Raja Janak ne kaam karte hue hi top achieve kiya. Aur tum dusron ke liye example bhi ho."}, "3.21": {"en": "People copy what leaders do. Whatever standard you set, others will follow. Be a good influence.", "hi": "Log leaders ko copy karte hain. Jo standard tum set karoge, log follow karenge. Achha influence bano."}, "3.22": {"en": "Krishna: \"I have nothing left to achieve, and I still keep working.\" Ultimate role model.", "hi": "Krishna: \"Mujhe kuch achieve nahi karna, phir bhi main kaam karta hoon.\" Ultimate role model."}, "3.23": {"en": "\"If I stopped working, everyone would copy me and stop too.\"", "hi": "\"Agar main kaam rok doon, toh sab mujhe copy karke ruk jaayenge.\""}, "3.24": {"en": "\"If I quit, the world falls into chaos.\" When people look up to you, your actions matter.", "hi": "\"Main ruk gaya toh duniya mein chaos ho jaayega.\" Jab log tumhe dekhte hain, tumhara action matter karta hai."}, "3.25": {"en": "Others work for personal gain. The wise work just as hard, but for the good of everyone.", "hi": "Dusre apne fayde ke liye kaam karte hain. Samajhdaar utni hi mehnat karte hain, par sabke bhale ke liye."}, "3.26": {"en": "Don't confuse people who are still learning. Lead by doing, not by lecturing.", "hi": "Jo abhi seekh rahe hain unhe confuse mat karo. Lecture nahi, karke dikhao."}, "3.27": {"en": "Nature is doing most of the work. Ego just jumps in and says \"I did this.\"", "hi": "Zyada kaam nature karti hai. Ego beech mein aake kehta hai \"maine kiya.\""}, "3.28": {"en": "Understand how nature works, and you stop taking everything personally. No attachment.", "hi": "Nature kaise kaam karti hai ye samjho, toh har cheez personally lena band ho jaata hai."}, "3.29": {"en": "People stuck in their patterns need patience, not judgement. Don't shake them up unnecessarily.", "hi": "Jo apne patterns mein phanse hain, unhe patience chahiye, judgement nahi. Bina wajah unhe mat hilao."}, "3.30": {"en": "Hand over your actions to me, drop the ego and anxiety, and do what needs doing. Calmly.", "hi": "Apne karm mujhe saunp do, ego aur anxiety chhodo, aur jo karna hai woh karo. Shaanti se."}, "3.31": {"en": "Those who live this with trust and without overthinking it are set free.", "hi": "Jo isko bharose ke saath jeete hain, bina overthinking ke, woh free ho jaate hain."}, "3.32": {"en": "Those who mock it and ignore it miss out completely. Their loss.", "hi": "Jo iska mazaak udaate hain aur ignore karte hain, woh sab miss kar dete hain. Unka nuksaan."}, "3.33": {"en": "Everyone acts according to their nature, even smart people. Suppressing it doesn't work. Channel it instead.", "hi": "Har koi apni nature ke hisaab se chalta hai, smart log bhi. Dabaana kaam nahi karta. Sahi direction do."}, "3.34": {"en": "Likes and dislikes are built into your senses. Don't let them boss you around. They're your enemies.", "hi": "Pasand-naapasand senses mein built-in hai. Unhe apna boss mat banne do. Woh tumhare dushman hain."}, "3.35": {"en": "Your own path done imperfectly beats someone else's done perfectly. Stop copy-pasting lives off your feed.", "hi": "Apna raasta imperfect bhi better hai, kisi aur ka perfect copy karne se. Feed se life copy-paste mat karo."}, "3.36": {"en": "Arjuna: \"Why do we do wrong things even when we don't want to?\" Most relatable question ever.", "hi": "Arjun: \"Hum na chahte hue bhi galat kaam kyun kar dete hain?\" Sabse relatable sawaal."}, "3.37": {"en": "Krishna: \"It's desire, and the anger that follows it. That's the real enemy.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Ye desire hai, aur uske baad aane wala gussa. Asli dushman yahi hai.\""}, "3.38": {"en": "Like smoke over fire or dust on a mirror, desire covers up your clarity.", "hi": "Jaise aag pe dhuaan ya sheeshe pe dhool, waise desire tumhari clarity ko dhak deta hai."}, "3.39": {"en": "Desire is never satisfied. Feed it and it just wants more. It blocks your wisdom.", "hi": "Desire kabhi satisfy nahi hota. Jitna khilao, utna aur maangta hai. Gyaan ko block kar deta hai."}, "3.40": {"en": "Desire hides in your senses, mind and thinking. That's how it takes over.", "hi": "Desire tumhare senses, mind aur soch mein chhupa rehta hai. Aise hi control le leta hai."}, "3.41": {"en": "So start with your senses. Get them in check and take down desire early.", "hi": "Toh senses se shuru karo. Unhe control karo aur desire ko jaldi khatam karo."}, "3.42": {"en": "Senses are strong, the mind is stronger, the intellect stronger still. The real you is above it all.", "hi": "Senses strong hain, mind usse strong, buddhi usse bhi strong. Asli tum sabse upar ho."}, "3.43": {"en": "Know who you really are, steady your mind, and defeat desire. Tough enemy, but beatable.", "hi": "Jaano tum asli mein kaun ho, mind steady karo, aur desire ko haraao. Mushkil dushman, par haar sakta hai."}, "4.1": {"en": "Krishna: \"I taught this wisdom ages ago to the Sun god, who passed it down.\" This isn't new content. It's timeless.", "hi": "Krishna: \"Ye gyaan maine bahut pehle Surya dev ko diya tha, unhone aage pass kiya.\" Ye naya content nahi, timeless hai."}, "4.2": {"en": "Wise kings passed it down for generations, but over time it got lost. Even great wisdom fades if nobody lives it.", "hi": "Raja log peedhi dar peedhi isse aage badhate rahe, par time ke saath ye kho gaya. Jo jiya na jaaye, woh gyaan bhi kho jaata hai."}, "4.3": {"en": "\"I'm sharing this secret with you because you're my friend and you're open to it.\"", "hi": "\"Ye secret main tumhe isliye bata raha hoon kyunki tum mere dost ho aur seekhne ko ready ho.\""}, "4.4": {"en": "Arjuna: \"Wait, you were born way after the Sun god. How did you teach him?\" Fair plot-hole check.", "hi": "Arjun: \"Ruko, aap toh Surya dev ke bahut baad paida hue. Aapne unhe kaise sikhaya?\" Fair plot-hole check."}, "4.5": {"en": "Krishna: \"We've both lived many lives. I remember all of mine. You don't remember yours.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Hum dono ke kai janam ho chuke hain. Mujhe sab yaad hain, tumhe nahi.\""}, "4.6": {"en": "\"I'm never truly born and I never change, but I choose to appear in the world through my own power.\"", "hi": "\"Main sach mein kabhi paida nahi hota aur kabhi badalta nahi, par apni shakti se duniya mein aana choose karta hoon.\""}, "4.7": {"en": "Whenever the world gets really messed up and goodness is losing, I show up. Hope is always loading.", "hi": "Jab duniya mein sab ulta-pulta ho jaata hai aur achhai haarne lagti hai, main aata hoon. Umeed hamesha loading hai."}, "4.8": {"en": "\"I come back in every age to protect good people, stop the harmful ones, and reset what's right.\"", "hi": "\"Har yug mein main aata hoon, achhe logon ko bachane, bure ko rokne aur sahi ko wapas set karne.\""}, "4.9": {"en": "Truly understand who Krishna is, and you won't be stuck in the cycle again. You'll reach him.", "hi": "Krishna ko sach mein samajh lo, toh dobara cycle mein nahi phansoge. Unhi tak pahunchoge."}, "4.10": {"en": "Free from craving, fear and anger, fully focused on the Divine, many people have already made it. You can too.", "hi": "Craving, darr aur gusse se free, poori tarah Bhagwan pe focused, kai log pahunch chuke hain. Tum bhi pahunch sakte ho."}, "4.11": {"en": "However you come to me, I meet you there. Every path people take leads to me in the end.", "hi": "Tum jaise bhi mere paas aao, main waise hi milta hoon. Har raasta aakhir mujh tak aata hai."}, "4.12": {"en": "People who want quick results pray for quick rewards, and they often get them. But quick isn't lasting.", "hi": "Jinhe jaldi result chahiye, woh jaldi wale rewards maangte hain, aur aksar mil bhi jaate hain. Par jaldi wala tikta nahi."}, "4.13": {"en": "People have different natures and strengths, so they do different work. Your role comes from who you are, not your label.", "hi": "Logon ki nature aur strengths alag hain, isliye kaam alag hai. Tumhara role tumhari nature se aata hai, label se nahi."}, "4.14": {"en": "\"Actions don't stick to me because I don't crave results.\" Get this and your work stops weighing you down.", "hi": "\"Karm mujh pe chipakte nahi kyunki mujhe result ki chahat nahi.\" Ye samjho, toh kaam bojh nahi lagega."}, "4.15": {"en": "Wise people before you worked this way and found freedom. So follow their lead and do your work.", "hi": "Tumse pehle samajhdaar logon ne aise hi kaam karke freedom paayi. Toh unke footsteps follow karo aur kaam karo."}, "4.16": {"en": "What counts as action? What counts as doing nothing? Even smart people get confused. Krishna's about to explain.", "hi": "Action kya hai? Kuch na karna kya hai? Smart log bhi confuse hote hain. Krishna ab samjhayenge."}, "4.17": {"en": "Right action, wrong action, and no action all need to be understood. The way of action is deep.", "hi": "Sahi karm, galat karm aur akarm, teeno ko samajhna padta hai. Karm ka raasta gehra hai."}, "4.18": {"en": "Being busy isn't always action, and being still isn't always idle. See through that and you're wise.", "hi": "Busy rehna hamesha action nahi hota, aur shaant baithna hamesha idle nahi. Ye dekh liya toh tum wise ho."}, "4.19": {"en": "Someone whose work has no selfish agenda, whose actions are cleansed by understanding, is truly wise.", "hi": "Jiske kaam mein koi selfish agenda nahi, jiske karm samajh se shuddh hain, wahi asli gyaani hai."}, "4.20": {"en": "Drop the obsession with results, feel complete within, depend on no one. You're working, but it doesn't bind you.", "hi": "Result ka obsession chhodo, andar se complete raho, kisi pe depend mat raho. Kaam karte ho, par woh baandhta nahi."}, "4.21": {"en": "No cravings, mind in control, no hoarding. Just doing what's needed. Nothing bad sticks to you.", "hi": "Na craving, mind control mein, na jama karne ki aadat. Bas zaroori kaam. Kuch bura chipakta nahi."}, "4.22": {"en": "Happy with what comes, unbothered by ups and downs, no jealousy. You act, but stay free.", "hi": "Jo mile usme khush, ups-downs se unbothered, koi jealousy nahi. Kaam karte ho, par free rehte ho."}, "4.23": {"en": "When attachment is gone and work becomes an offering, your karma just melts away.", "hi": "Jab attachment chala jaaye aur kaam offering ban jaaye, toh karma pighal jaata hai."}, "4.24": {"en": "See the divine in everything: the offering, the act, the one who offers, the goal. Then every task becomes sacred.", "hi": "Har cheez mein divine dekho: offering, kaam, karne wala, goal. Tab har kaam pavitra ban jaata hai."}, "4.25": {"en": "Some people worship through rituals, others through pure understanding. There's more than one way to give.", "hi": "Kuch log rituals se pooja karte hain, kuch gyaan se. Dene ke kai tareeke hain."}, "4.26": {"en": "Some practice self-control over their senses, others enjoy the world mindfully. Both can be offerings.", "hi": "Kuch senses pe control practice karte hain, kuch mindfully duniya enjoy karte hain. Dono offering ho sakte hain."}, "4.27": {"en": "Some offer their senses and breath into the fire of a disciplined mind. Self-control as worship.", "hi": "Kuch apne senses aur saans ko disciplined mind ki aag mein arpan karte hain. Self-control bhi pooja hai."}, "4.28": {"en": "Some give wealth, some do tough discipline, some practise yoga, some study deeply. All count if done sincerely.", "hi": "Koi daan karta hai, koi tapasya, koi yoga, koi gehri padhai. Sab count hota hai agar dil se kiya ho."}, "4.29": {"en": "Some focus on mindful eating and breathwork. Even breathing can become a spiritual practice.", "hi": "Kuch mindful khaane aur breathwork pe focus karte hain. Saans lena bhi spiritual practice ban sakta hai."}, "4.30": {"en": "All of them understand what giving means, and giving cleans them up. That's how they move forward.", "hi": "Ye sab samajhte hain ki dena kya hota hai, aur dene se woh saaf hote hain. Aise hi aage badhte hain."}, "4.31": {"en": "If you never give anything, even this life won't work out for you, let alone the next.", "hi": "Agar kabhi kuch nahi dete, toh ye life bhi theek nahi chalegi, agle ki toh baat hi chhodo."}, "4.32": {"en": "There are many ways of giving, and all involve action. Understand that and you're free.", "hi": "Dene ke kai tareeke hain, aur sabme action hai. Ye samajh lo toh tum free ho."}, "4.33": {"en": "Sharing wisdom beats sharing stuff. All action ultimately leads to understanding.", "hi": "Gyaan baantna cheezein baantne se bada hai. Har karm aakhir mein samajh tak le jaata hai."}, "4.34": {"en": "Find a real teacher. Be humble, ask questions, and help out. That's how wisdom gets passed on.", "hi": "Ek sachcha guru dhoondo. Humble raho, sawaal poocho, seva karo. Gyaan aise hi milta hai."}, "4.35": {"en": "Once you get it, you won't be confused like this again. You'll see everyone as part of you, and you in me.", "hi": "Ek baar samajh gaye, toh aise confuse nahi hoge. Sabko apna hissa dekhoge, aur khud ko mujh mein."}, "4.36": {"en": "Even if you've made the worst mistakes, wisdom is a boat that gets you across. Nobody's beyond saving.", "hi": "Chahe sabse bade galti ki ho, gyaan ek naav hai jo paar le jaati hai. Koi bhi bachne se bahar nahi."}, "4.37": {"en": "Like fire burns wood to ash, real understanding burns up your past karma.", "hi": "Jaise aag lakdi ko raakh kar deti hai, waise asli samajh purane karma ko jala deti hai."}, "4.38": {"en": "Nothing cleanses you like wisdom. Keep doing your work right, and it shows up within you in time.", "hi": "Gyaan jaisa kuch saaf nahi karta. Apna kaam sahi karte raho, time ke saath ye andar se aa jaata hai."}, "4.39": {"en": "Trust it, stay committed, control your senses, and wisdom comes. With it comes deep peace, fast.", "hi": "Bharosa rakho, committed raho, senses control karo, gyaan aayega. Saath mein gehri shaanti bhi, jaldi."}, "4.40": {"en": "Constant doubt with no trust leaves you with nothing, here or anywhere. Overthinking everything kills happiness.", "hi": "Hamesha shak aur bharosa zero, toh na yahan kuch milta hai na kahin aur. Har cheez pe overthinking khushi maar deti hai."}, "4.41": {"en": "Work without attachment, clear your doubts with understanding, stay grounded. Then actions can't trap you.", "hi": "Bina attachment kaam karo, samajh se doubts clear karo, grounded raho. Tab karm tumhe phansa nahi sakte."}, "4.42": {"en": "Cut through your doubt with the sword of wisdom. Now stand up and do what you need to do.", "hi": "Gyaan ki talwaar se apna doubt kaat do. Ab utho aur jo karna hai woh karo."}, "5.1": {"en": "Arjuna: \"You praise quitting action, then you praise doing action. Which one's actually better?\"", "hi": "Arjun: \"Aap karm chhodne ki taareef karte ho, phir karm karne ki. Asli mein better kaun sa hai?\""}, "5.2": {"en": "Krishna: \"Both get you there, but doing your work selflessly beats just dropping everything.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Dono pahunchate hain, par selflessly kaam karna sab chhod dene se better hai.\""}, "5.3": {"en": "Someone who doesn't hate or crave, and isn't tossed by ups and downs, has already let go. They're free.", "hi": "Jo na nafrat karta hai na craving, ups-downs se nahi hilta, woh pehle hi chhod chuka hai. Woh free hai."}, "5.4": {"en": "Only beginners think knowledge and action are rivals. Commit fully to one and you get the benefits of both.", "hi": "Sirf beginners sochte hain ki gyaan aur karm rivals hain. Ek mein poora commit karo, dono ka fayda milega."}, "5.5": {"en": "Thinkers and doers reach the same place. Whoever sees they're one path really gets it.", "hi": "Sochne wale aur karne wale ek hi jagah pahunchte hain. Jo dekh le ki dono ek hain, wahi samjha."}, "5.6": {"en": "Trying to renounce everything without first doing the work is really hard. Act selflessly and you'll get there faster.", "hi": "Bina kaam kiye sab chhodna bahut mushkil hai. Selflessly kaam karo, jaldi pahunchoge."}, "5.7": {"en": "Clean heart, self-control, and seeing yourself in everyone. Then even while working, nothing sticks to you.", "hi": "Saaf dil, self-control, aur sab mein khud ko dekhna. Tab kaam karte hue bhi kuch chipakta nahi."}, "5.8": {"en": "Seeing, hearing, eating, walking, sleeping. The wise know it's the senses doing their thing, not ego.", "hi": "Dekhna, sunna, khaana, chalna, sona. Samajhdaar jaante hain ki ye senses ka kaam hai, ego ka nahi."}, "5.9": {"en": "Talking, blinking, grabbing stuff: it's all senses meeting the world. You're the witness, not the ego.", "hi": "Bolna, palak jhapakna, kuch pakadna: ye sab senses aur duniya ka milna hai. Tum dekhne wale ho, ego nahi."}, "5.10": {"en": "Act without attachment and offer it up, and nothing bad sticks, like water off a lotus leaf.", "hi": "Bina attachment kaam karo aur arpan kar do, kuch bura nahi chipkega, jaise kamal ke patte pe paani."}, "5.11": {"en": "Yogis use body, mind and senses to work, but only to purify themselves, not to get stuff.", "hi": "Yogi body, mind aur senses se kaam karte hain, par khud ko shuddh karne ke liye, kuch paane ke liye nahi."}, "5.12": {"en": "Let go of the results and you find lasting peace. Chase the results and you stay stuck.", "hi": "Result chhodo toh lasting peace milti hai. Result ke peeche bhaago toh phanse rehte ho."}, "5.13": {"en": "Your body is like a house with nine doors. Live in it calmly, without claiming credit for everything.", "hi": "Tumhara body nau darwazon wala ghar hai. Usme shaanti se raho, har cheez ka credit liye bina."}, "5.14": {"en": "Your true self doesn't create the drama of doing or the results. Your habits and nature run that show.", "hi": "Asli tum karne ya result ka drama nahi banate. Woh show tumhari aadatein aur nature chalati hain."}, "5.15": {"en": "God isn't keeping score of your sins and good deeds. Confusion just hides the truth from us.", "hi": "Bhagwan tumhare paap-punya ka score nahi rakh rahe. Bas confusion sach ko chhupa deta hai."}, "5.16": {"en": "When real understanding wipes out that confusion, the truth shines like the sun.", "hi": "Jab asli samajh confusion ko mita deti hai, toh sach suraj ki tarah chamakta hai."}, "5.17": {"en": "Make the highest truth your focus, think about it, commit to it, and you'll reach a place you never fall back from.", "hi": "Sabse ooncha sach apna focus banao, uske baare mein socho, commit karo, aur aisi jagah pahunchoge jahan se wapas nahi girte."}, "5.18": {"en": "The wise see the same soul in a scholar, a cow, an elephant, a dog and an outcast. No hierarchy.", "hi": "Samajhdaar ko scholar, gaay, haathi, kutte aur outcast sab mein ek hi aatma dikhti hai. Koi hierarchy nahi."}, "5.19": {"en": "See everyone as equal, and you've already won at life, right here, right now.", "hi": "Sabko barabar dekho, toh life tum yahin, abhi jeet chuke ho."}, "5.20": {"en": "Don't get hyped by good news or crushed by bad news. Stay steady and clear.", "hi": "Achhi news pe hype mat ho, buri news pe toot mat jao. Steady aur clear raho."}, "5.21": {"en": "Stop needing outside things for happiness. Find joy within and it lasts forever.", "hi": "Khushi ke liye bahar ki cheezon pe depend karna chhodo. Andar se khushi dhoondo, woh hamesha rahegi."}, "5.22": {"en": "Pleasures from the senses start and end, and leave pain behind. The wise don't get hooked.", "hi": "Senses wale maze shuru aur khatam hote hain, aur dard chhod jaate hain. Samajhdaar unme phanste nahi."}, "5.23": {"en": "If you can handle the rush of desire and anger in this life, you're a real yogi and truly happy.", "hi": "Agar is life mein desire aur gusse ka rush handle kar sakte ho, toh tum asli yogi ho aur sach mein khush ho."}, "5.24": {"en": "Joy inside, peace inside, light inside. That person has found the ultimate happiness.", "hi": "Andar khushi, andar shaanti, andar roshni. Usne sabse badi khushi paa li."}, "5.25": {"en": "Calm, self-controlled, free from extremes and working for everyone's good. That's how you find bliss.", "hi": "Shaant, self-controlled, extremes se free, aur sabke bhale ke liye kaam karna. Aise bliss milta hai."}, "5.26": {"en": "Free from desire and anger, mind under control. For those people, peace is right there.", "hi": "Desire aur gusse se free, mind control mein. Aise logon ke liye peace bilkul paas hai."}, "5.27": {"en": "Block out distractions, focus your gaze between your eyebrows, balance your breath. Meditation 101.", "hi": "Distractions band karo, nazar bhauhon ke beech, saans balance karo. Meditation 101."}, "5.28": {"en": "Senses, mind and intellect in control, freedom as the goal, no desire, fear or anger. That person is already free.", "hi": "Senses, mind aur buddhi control mein, goal freedom, na desire, na darr, na gussa. Woh pehle se free hai."}, "5.29": {"en": "Know that I'm the friend of every being and the one behind all good effort. That's where peace comes from.", "hi": "Jaano ki main har jeev ka dost hoon aur har achhe effort ke peeche hoon. Peace wahin se aati hai."}, "6.1": {"en": "A real renunciate isn't someone who quits everything. It's someone who does their duty without chasing rewards.", "hi": "Asli sanyasi woh nahi jo sab chhod de. Woh hai jo reward ke peeche bhaage bina apna kaam kare."}, "6.2": {"en": "Letting go and selfless work are the same thing. You can't do either while still chasing what you want.", "hi": "Chhodna aur selfless kaam ek hi cheez hai. Apni chahat ke peeche bhaagte hue dono nahi ho sakte."}, "6.3": {"en": "When you're starting out, action is the way. Once you've leveled up, calm is the way.", "hi": "Shuruaat mein action hi raasta hai. Level up hone ke baad shaanti raasta hai."}, "6.4": {"en": "When you stop clinging to sense pleasures and to your actions, you've reached the top of yoga.", "hi": "Jab sense ke mazon aur apne karm se chipakna band ho jaaye, tab tum yoga ke top pe ho."}, "6.5": {"en": "You can be your own best friend or your own worst enemy. Lift yourself up. Don't drag yourself down.", "hi": "Tum khud ke best friend bhi ho aur worst enemy bhi. Khud ko upar uthao, neeche mat kheecho."}, "6.6": {"en": "Master your mind and it becomes your best friend. Leave it untamed and it acts like your enemy.", "hi": "Mind ko master karo toh woh best friend banta hai. Bekaabu chhodo toh dushman ki tarah behave karta hai."}, "6.7": {"en": "With a calm, controlled mind you stay steady through heat or cold, praise or insults.", "hi": "Shaant aur controlled mind ke saath garmi-sardi, taareef-beizzati sab mein steady rehte ho."}, "6.8": {"en": "To someone truly at peace, dirt, stone and gold are all the same. Status doesn't move them.", "hi": "Jo sach mein shaant hai, uske liye mitti, patthar aur sona sab same hai. Status unhe hila nahi sakta."}, "6.9": {"en": "Friends, haters, family, strangers, good people and bad: treat them all with the same fairness. That's next level.", "hi": "Dost, haters, family, ajnabi, achhe aur bure: sabke saath ek jaisa insaaf. Ye next level hai."}, "6.10": {"en": "Find some alone time daily. Quiet your thoughts, drop your wants, and just focus.", "hi": "Roz thoda alone time nikaalo. Thoughts shaant karo, chahatein chhodo, aur bas focus karo."}, "6.11": {"en": "Set up a clean, comfortable spot, not too high or too low. Your meditation space matters.", "hi": "Ek saaf, comfortable jagah set karo, na zyada oonchi na neechi. Meditation space matter karta hai."}, "6.12": {"en": "Sit there, focus your mind, control your senses, and practise to clear your inner self.", "hi": "Wahan baitho, mind focus karo, senses control karo, aur andar ki safai ke liye practice karo."}, "6.13": {"en": "Back, neck and head straight. Stay still. Soft focus on the tip of your nose. No looking around.", "hi": "Kamar, gardan aur sar seedhe. Stable raho. Naak ki nok pe halka focus. Idhar-udhar mat dekho."}, "6.14": {"en": "Stay calm and fearless, keep your discipline, and focus your mind on the Divine.", "hi": "Shaant aur nidar raho, discipline banaye rakho, aur mind ko Bhagwan pe focus karo."}, "6.15": {"en": "Practise like this regularly and you'll reach a peace that's the highest kind there is.", "hi": "Aise regular practice karo toh woh peace milegi jo sabse oonchi hai."}, "6.16": {"en": "Overeating or starving, oversleeping or pulling all-nighters: none of it works. Balance is the key.", "hi": "Zyada khaana ya bhookha rehna, zyada sona ya raat bhar jaagna: kuch kaam nahi karta. Balance hi key hai."}, "6.17": {"en": "Balanced food, fun, work and sleep. That's how yoga actually ends your stress.", "hi": "Balanced khaana, masti, kaam aur neend. Aise hi yoga sach mein stress khatam karta hai."}, "6.18": {"en": "When your mind rests in your true self and stops craving stuff, you're ready for real yoga.", "hi": "Jab mind apne asli self mein tike aur cheezon ki craving band ho, tab tum asli yoga ke liye ready ho."}, "6.19": {"en": "Like a candle flame that doesn't flicker in a room with no wind. That's a focused mind.", "hi": "Jaise bina hawa wale kamre mein deepak ki lau nahi hilti. Waisa hota hai focused mind."}, "6.20": {"en": "When practice settles the mind, you see your true self and feel joy just from that.", "hi": "Jab practice se mind settle hota hai, toh asli self dikhta hai aur usi se khushi milti hai."}, "6.21": {"en": "There's a happiness beyond the senses that only a clear mind can feel. Once you find it, you don't slip.", "hi": "Ek khushi hai jo senses se pare hai, sirf clear mind feel kar sakta hai. Ek baar mil gayi toh fisalte nahi."}, "6.22": {"en": "Once you've got it, nothing else compares. Even the hardest pain can't shake you.", "hi": "Ek baar mil gaya toh kuch aur compare nahi karta. Sabse bada dard bhi hila nahi sakta."}, "6.23": {"en": "Yoga is literally disconnecting from suffering. Practise it with determination. Don't give up.", "hi": "Yoga ka matlab hai dukh se disconnect hona. Isse determination se practice karo. Haar mat maano."}, "6.24": {"en": "Drop the wants your mind keeps cooking up, and pull your senses back from every direction.", "hi": "Mind jo chahatein bana raha hai unhe chhodo, aur senses ko har taraf se wapas kheencho."}, "6.25": {"en": "Slowly, step by step, steady your mind with willpower and focus only on your true self.", "hi": "Dheere dheere, step by step, willpower se mind steady karo aur sirf apne asli self pe focus karo."}, "6.26": {"en": "Mind wandering again? Totally normal. Gently bring it back, every single time. That's the whole practice.", "hi": "Mind phir bhaag gaya? Normal hai. Pyaar se wapas lao, har baar. Bas yahi practice hai."}, "6.27": {"en": "Calm mind, no restlessness, no guilt. That yogi finds the highest happiness.", "hi": "Shaant mind, na bechaini, na guilt. Aise yogi ko sabse badi khushi milti hai."}, "6.28": {"en": "Keep practising and stay clean inside, and supreme joy comes easily.", "hi": "Practice karte raho aur andar se saaf raho, toh sabse badi khushi aasaani se milti hai."}, "6.29": {"en": "With a focused mind you see yourself in everyone and everyone in yourself. We're all connected.", "hi": "Focused mind se tum sab mein khud ko aur khud mein sabko dekhte ho. Hum sab connected hain."}, "6.30": {"en": "See me in everyone and everyone in me, and we'll never lose each other.", "hi": "Mujhe sab mein aur sabko mujh mein dekho, toh hum kabhi ek dusre ko nahi khoyenge."}, "6.31": {"en": "Love the Divine in every being, and however you live, you stay connected to me.", "hi": "Har jeev mein Bhagwan ko pyaar karo, phir chahe jaise bhi jiyo, mujhse jude rahoge."}, "6.32": {"en": "Feel others' pain and joy as your own. That empathy is the highest kind of yoga.", "hi": "Dusron ka dukh-sukh apna samjho. Yahi empathy sabse ooncha yoga hai."}, "6.33": {"en": "Arjuna: \"This sounds great, but my mind is all over the place. How do I keep it steady?\"", "hi": "Arjun: \"Sunne mein achha hai, par mera mind idhar-udhar bhaagta hai. Steady kaise rakhun?\""}, "6.34": {"en": "\"The mind is restless, stubborn and strong. Controlling it feels like trying to control the wind.\" So relatable.", "hi": "\"Mind bechain, ziddi aur strong hai. Isse control karna hawa ko control karne jaisa lagta hai.\" Bahut relatable."}, "6.35": {"en": "Krishna: \"True, it's tough. But with practice and letting go, you can train it.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Sach hai, mushkil hai. Par practice aur detachment se ise train kar sakte ho.\""}, "6.36": {"en": "Without self-control yoga's hard. But with effort and the right method, anyone can do it.", "hi": "Bina self-control yoga mushkil hai. Par effort aur sahi tareeke se koi bhi kar sakta hai."}, "6.37": {"en": "Arjuna: \"What if someone tries with faith but slips up and doesn't make it? What happens to them?\"", "hi": "Arjun: \"Agar koi bharose se try kare par fisal jaaye aur na pahunch paaye? Uska kya hoga?\""}, "6.38": {"en": "\"Do they lose both worlds and just vanish, like a cloud torn apart?\" The fear of failing halfway.", "hi": "\"Kya woh dono duniya kho ke gayab ho jaata hai, jaise phata hua baadal?\" Beech mein fail hone ka darr."}, "6.39": {"en": "\"Krishna, only you can clear this doubt. Please answer.\"", "hi": "\"Krishna, ye doubt sirf aap clear kar sakte ho. Please bataiye.\""}, "6.40": {"en": "Krishna: \"Nobody who tries to do good ever ends up lost. Not here, not after.\" Effort is never wasted.", "hi": "Krishna: \"Jo achha karne ki koshish karta hai, woh kabhi khota nahi. Na yahan, na baad mein.\" Effort kabhi waste nahi."}, "6.41": {"en": "They're reborn into a good, comfortable family to keep going. The universe saves your progress.", "hi": "Woh achhi, sukhi family mein phir paida hote hain taaki aage badh sakein. Universe tumhara progress save rakhta hai."}, "6.42": {"en": "Or they're born into a family of wise people. That's a rare blessing.", "hi": "Ya gyaani logon ki family mein janam lete hain. Ye rare blessing hai."}, "6.43": {"en": "They pick up the wisdom from their past life and push even harder. Like loading a saved game.", "hi": "Pichhle janam ka gyaan wapas mil jaata hai aur woh aur mehnat karte hain. Jaise saved game load karna."}, "6.44": {"en": "Past practice pulls them forward almost automatically. Even curiosity about yoga lifts you higher.", "hi": "Purani practice unhe apne aap aage kheenchti hai. Yoga ke baare mein curiosity bhi tumhe upar uthati hai."}, "6.45": {"en": "Keep striving sincerely, life after life, and you'll reach the highest goal.", "hi": "Dil se koshish karte raho, janam dar janam, aur sabse ooncha goal paa loge."}, "6.46": {"en": "A yogi beats someone who only does tough discipline, only studies, or only does rituals. So be a yogi.", "hi": "Yogi sirf tapasya, sirf padhai ya sirf rituals karne walon se aage hai. Toh yogi bano."}, "6.47": {"en": "And of all yogis, the one who loves me with full faith and heart is the closest to me.", "hi": "Aur sab yogiyon mein, jo poore bharose aur dil se mujhe pyaar karta hai, woh mere sabse kareeb hai."}, "7.1": {"en": "Krishna: \"Keep your mind on me and practise, and I'll show you how to know me completely.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Mind mujh pe rakho aur practice karo, main batata hoon mujhe poori tarah kaise jaano.\""}, "7.2": {"en": "\"I'll give you the full knowledge and the lived experience. After this, there's nothing left to figure out.\"", "hi": "\"Main tumhe poora gyaan aur uska anubhav dunga. Iske baad kuch samajhna baaki nahi rahega.\""}, "7.3": {"en": "Out of thousands, a few try. Out of those trying, very few truly get it. Rare, but possible.", "hi": "Hazaaron mein se kuch koshish karte hain. Unme se bahut kam sach mein samajhte hain. Rare hai, par possible."}, "7.4": {"en": "Earth, water, fire, air, space, mind, intellect, ego: these eight make up my material side.", "hi": "Dharti, paani, aag, hawa, aakash, mind, buddhi, ego: ye aath mera material side hain."}, "7.5": {"en": "That's my lower nature. My higher nature is the life force that keeps the whole universe running.", "hi": "Ye meri neeche wali nature hai. Oonchi nature woh life force hai jo poore universe ko chalati hai."}, "7.6": {"en": "Matter plus life force creates everything. And I'm the source and the end of it all.", "hi": "Matter aur life force milke sab banate hain. Aur sabka shuru aur ant main hoon."}, "7.7": {"en": "Nothing is higher than me. Everything is strung on me like pearls on a thread.", "hi": "Mujhse ooncha kuch nahi. Sab kuch mujh mein aise piroya hai jaise dhaage mein moti."}, "7.8": {"en": "I'm the taste of water, the light of the sun and moon, the Om in prayers. Look closely and you'll see me everywhere.", "hi": "Main paani ka swaad, suraj-chaand ki roshni, prarthana ka Om hoon. Dhyaan se dekho, main har jagah hoon."}, "7.9": {"en": "I'm the fresh smell of earth, the heat in fire, the life in every being, the discipline in the disciplined.", "hi": "Main mitti ki khushboo, aag ki garmi, har jeev ki jaan, aur tapasvi ka discipline hoon."}, "7.10": {"en": "I'm the original seed of all beings, the intelligence of the smart, and the shine of the brilliant.", "hi": "Main sab jeevon ka asli beej, samajhdaar ki buddhi, aur talented ki chamak hoon."}, "7.11": {"en": "I'm strength without greed, and desire that doesn't go against what's right. Healthy ambition is divine.", "hi": "Main bina laalach wali taakat hoon, aur woh chahat jo dharm ke khilaaf nahi. Healthy ambition bhi divine hai."}, "7.12": {"en": "Every mood, calm, restless or lazy, comes from me. But I'm not trapped in them; they're in me.", "hi": "Har mood, shaant, bechain ya aalsi, mujhse aata hai. Par main unme phansa nahi; woh mujh mein hain."}, "7.13": {"en": "People get so caught up in their moods that they miss what's beyond them: me.", "hi": "Log apne moods mein itna phans jaate hain ki unke pare jo hai, yaani mujhe, miss kar dete hain."}, "7.14": {"en": "This illusion is hard to escape. But those who turn to me get through it.", "hi": "Ye maya se bachna mushkil hai. Par jo meri sharan aate hain, woh paar ho jaate hain."}, "7.15": {"en": "People who keep doing harm, lost in confusion and ego, don't turn to me. They're stuck.", "hi": "Jo log nuksaan karte rehte hain, confusion aur ego mein khoye hain, woh meri taraf nahi aate. Woh phanse hain."}, "7.16": {"en": "Four kinds of good people turn to me: those in pain, the curious, those who need help, and the wise.", "hi": "Chaar tarah ke achhe log mere paas aate hain: dukhi, jigyasu, zaroorat wale, aur gyaani."}, "7.17": {"en": "Of these, the wise one who loves me for my own sake is the best. We're very dear to each other.", "hi": "Inme se jo gyaani bina kisi wajah mujhe pyaar karta hai, woh sabse best hai. Hum ek dusre ko bahut pyaare hain."}, "7.18": {"en": "All of them are good, but the wise one feels like my own self. They want nothing but me.", "hi": "Sab achhe hain, par gyaani mujhe apna hi roop lagta hai. Use mere siva kuch nahi chahiye."}, "7.19": {"en": "After many lives, the wise realise \"the Divine is everything\" and come to me. Such souls are rare.", "hi": "Kai janam ke baad gyaani samajhte hain ki \"sab kuch Bhagwan hi hai\" aur mere paas aate hain. Aise log rare hain."}, "7.20": {"en": "People driven by wants turn to other gods for quick results, based on their own nature.", "hi": "Chahaton se chalne wale log jaldi result ke liye dusre devtaon ke paas jaate hain, apni nature ke hisaab se."}, "7.21": {"en": "Whatever form someone worships with faith, I make their faith stronger.", "hi": "Koi jis bhi roop ki pooja bharose se kare, main uska bharosa aur pakka kar deta hoon."}, "7.22": {"en": "They pray with faith and get what they want, but really, it's me giving it.", "hi": "Woh bharose se maangte hain aur unhe milta hai, par asli mein main hi de raha hoon."}, "7.23": {"en": "Those small rewards don't last. Aim for the gods and you reach them. Aim for me and you reach me.", "hi": "Woh chhote rewards tikte nahi. Devtaon ko aim karo toh unhe paoge. Mujhe aim karo toh mujhe paoge."}, "7.24": {"en": "People who don't get it think I'm just a person who showed up. They miss my unlimited side.", "hi": "Jo nahi samajhte, woh sochte hain main bas ek insaan hoon jo aa gaya. Mera unlimited side miss kar dete hain."}, "7.25": {"en": "I'm hidden behind illusion, so not everyone sees me. The world doesn't recognise that I'm eternal.", "hi": "Main maya ke peeche chhupa hoon, isliye sabko nahi dikhta. Duniya nahi pehchanti ki main hamesha hoon."}, "7.26": {"en": "I know everyone: past, present and future. But nobody truly knows me.", "hi": "Main sabko jaanta hoon: bhoot, vartmaan aur bhavishya. Par mujhe koi sach mein nahi jaanta."}, "7.27": {"en": "From birth, everyone gets trapped in love-hate cycles. That's what confuses us.", "hi": "Janam se hi sab pasand-naapasand ke cycle mein phans jaate hain. Yahi humein confuse karta hai."}, "7.28": {"en": "Those who keep doing good eventually break free of that cycle and commit to me fully.", "hi": "Jo achha karte rehte hain, woh aakhir mein us cycle se nikalte hain aur poori tarah mujhse jud jaate hain."}, "7.29": {"en": "Those who turn to me to get past ageing and death come to understand the whole truth.", "hi": "Jo budhape aur maut se paar jaane ke liye meri sharan aate hain, woh poora sach samajh jaate hain."}, "7.30": {"en": "Those who know me in every part of life keep remembering me, even at the very end.", "hi": "Jo mujhe life ke har hisse mein jaante hain, woh aakhri pal mein bhi mujhe yaad rakhte hain."}, "8.1": {"en": "Arjuna drops a list of deep questions: What's the ultimate reality? What's the self? What's karma?", "hi": "Arjun gehre sawaalon ki list deta hai: Ultimate reality kya hai? Self kya hai? Karma kya hai?"}, "8.2": {"en": "\"And how can someone remember you at the moment of death?\" The biggest question of all.", "hi": "\"Aur maut ke waqt koi aapko kaise yaad rakh sakta hai?\" Sabse bada sawaal."}, "8.3": {"en": "Krishna: \"The ultimate reality never changes. Your true nature is your self. Karma is the action that creates life.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Ultimate reality kabhi nahi badalti. Tumhari asli nature tumhara self hai. Karma woh action hai jo life banata hai.\""}, "8.4": {"en": "\"The physical world keeps changing. The cosmic spirit runs it. And I live inside every body.\"", "hi": "\"Physical duniya badalti rehti hai. Cosmic spirit use chalata hai. Aur main har body ke andar hoon.\""}, "8.5": {"en": "Whoever thinks of me at their last moment comes straight to me. No doubt about it.", "hi": "Jo aakhri pal mein mujhe yaad karta hai, woh seedha mere paas aata hai. Isme koi shak nahi."}, "8.6": {"en": "Whatever you think about most in life is what you'll think of at the end. And that's where you'll go.", "hi": "Life mein jo sabse zyada sochte ho, wahi aakhir mein yaad aata hai. Aur wahin pahunchte ho."}, "8.7": {"en": "So remember me all the time, and keep doing your work. Mind and heart on me, you'll reach me.", "hi": "Toh mujhe hamesha yaad rakho, aur apna kaam karte raho. Mind aur dil mujh pe, toh mujh tak pahunchoge."}, "8.8": {"en": "Practise focusing, don't let your mind drift, and you'll reach the supreme.", "hi": "Focus ki practice karo, mind ko bhatakne mat do, aur tum param tak pahunchoge."}, "8.9": {"en": "Meditate on the one who knows all, is ancient, subtle, shines like the sun and is beyond darkness.", "hi": "Us par dhyaan karo jo sab jaanta hai, sabse purana hai, sookshm hai, suraj jaisa chamakta hai aur andhere se pare hai."}, "8.10": {"en": "At the end, with a steady mind full of love and focus, you reach that supreme being.", "hi": "Aakhir mein steady mind, pyaar aur focus ke saath, tum us param tak pahunchte ho."}, "8.11": {"en": "Here's a quick summary of the ultimate goal that wise people work so hard to reach.", "hi": "Ab us ultimate goal ka short summary, jiske liye gyaani itni mehnat karte hain."}, "8.12": {"en": "Close off distractions, centre your mind in your heart, and stay steady in meditation.", "hi": "Distractions band karo, mind ko dil mein tikao, aur dhyaan mein steady raho."}, "8.13": {"en": "Chant Om and think of me as you leave your body, and you reach the highest goal.", "hi": "Body chhodte waqt Om japo aur mujhe yaad karo, toh sabse ooncha goal milta hai."}, "8.14": {"en": "For someone who remembers me constantly with full focus, I'm easy to reach.", "hi": "Jo mujhe lagataar poore focus se yaad karta hai, uske liye main aasaani se milta hoon."}, "8.15": {"en": "Those who reach me don't come back to a temporary world full of pain. They've made it.", "hi": "Jo mujh tak pahunchte hain, woh dukh bhari temporary duniya mein wapas nahi aate. Woh pahunch gaye."}, "8.16": {"en": "Every world, even the highest heaven, has a return ticket. Reach me and there's no return.", "hi": "Har lok, sabse ooncha swarg bhi, wapsi ka ticket hai. Mujh tak pahuncho toh wapsi nahi."}, "8.17": {"en": "A single day of the creator lasts thousands of ages. Our timeline is tiny on the cosmic scale.", "hi": "Brahma ka ek din hazaaron yugon ka hota hai. Cosmic scale pe hamari timeline bahut chhoti hai."}, "8.18": {"en": "When the cosmic day starts, everything appears. When cosmic night falls, everything dissolves.", "hi": "Jab cosmic din shuru hota hai, sab prakat hota hai. Jab cosmic raat aati hai, sab vileen ho jaata hai."}, "8.19": {"en": "Beings appear and disappear again and again, on repeat, with every cosmic day and night.", "hi": "Jeev baar-baar aate aur jaate hain, repeat pe, har cosmic din aur raat ke saath."}, "8.20": {"en": "But beyond all that is something eternal that never gets destroyed, even when everything else does.", "hi": "Par in sabke pare kuch hamesha rehne wala hai jo kabhi khatam nahi hota, jab sab kuch khatam ho jaaye tab bhi."}, "8.21": {"en": "That eternal state is my home. Once you reach it, you never come back.", "hi": "Woh hamesha wali state mera ghar hai. Ek baar pahuncho, toh wapas nahi aate."}, "8.22": {"en": "The supreme, who holds everything, is reached through pure, single-minded devotion.", "hi": "Jo param sab ko sambhale hai, woh sirf shuddh, ek-man bhakti se milta hai."}, "8.23": {"en": "Now I'll tell you about the two ways people leave this world: one with return, one without.", "hi": "Ab main batata hoon duniya chhodne ke do raaste: ek wapsi wala, ek bina wapsi."}, "8.24": {"en": "The path of light: those who know the truth take this route and don't come back.", "hi": "Roshni ka raasta: jo sach jaante hain woh is raaste se jaate hain aur wapas nahi aate."}, "8.25": {"en": "The path of smoke and darkness: those who take this route come back again.", "hi": "Dhuein aur andhere ka raasta: jo is raaste se jaate hain, woh phir lautte hain."}, "8.26": {"en": "Two eternal paths, light and dark. One leads out of the cycle, the other back into it.", "hi": "Do hamesha wale raaste, roshni aur andhera. Ek cycle se bahar le jaata hai, dusra wapas."}, "8.27": {"en": "A yogi who knows these paths isn't confused. So stay steady in yoga, always.", "hi": "Jo yogi ye raaste jaanta hai, woh confuse nahi hota. Toh hamesha yoga mein steady raho."}, "8.28": {"en": "Know this, and you go beyond all the rewards of rituals and good deeds to the supreme state.", "hi": "Ye jaan lo, toh rituals aur punya ke saare rewards se aage param state tak pahunchte ho."}, "9.1": {"en": "Krishna: \"Since you don't nitpick, I'll tell you the deepest secret. It'll free you.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Kyunki tum nukta-cheeni nahi karte, main tumhe sabse gehra raaz batata hoon. Ye tumhe free karega.\""}, "9.2": {"en": "This is the king of all knowledge. You can experience it directly, and it's actually enjoyable to practise.", "hi": "Ye gyaan ka raja hai. Iska seedha anubhav hota hai, aur practice karne mein maza bhi aata hai."}, "9.3": {"en": "People with zero faith in this keep going around in the cycle and never reach me.", "hi": "Jinhe isme bilkul bharosa nahi, woh cycle mein ghoomte rehte hain aur mujh tak nahi pahunchte."}, "9.4": {"en": "I'm in everything, unseen. Everything rests in me, but I'm not limited by any of it.", "hi": "Main sab mein hoon, bina dikhe. Sab mujh mein tika hai, par main kisi se limited nahi."}, "9.5": {"en": "I hold everything up, yet I'm not stuck in anything. That's my mystery.", "hi": "Main sab ko sambhalta hoon, par kisi mein phansa nahi. Yahi mera rahasya hai."}, "9.6": {"en": "Like wind moves through the sky but stays in the sky, all beings move within me.", "hi": "Jaise hawa aakash mein chalti hai par aakash mein hi rehti hai, waise sab jeev mujh mein chalte hain."}, "9.7": {"en": "At the end of a cosmic cycle everything returns to me, and at the start I send it out again.", "hi": "Cosmic cycle ke ant mein sab mujh mein lautta hai, aur shuru mein main phir se bhejta hoon."}, "9.8": {"en": "Through nature I create again and again. Beings follow nature's flow.", "hi": "Nature ke zariye main baar-baar banata hoon. Jeev nature ke flow ke saath chalte hain."}, "9.9": {"en": "None of this binds me, because I stay detached. Like a chill observer.", "hi": "Ye sab mujhe baandhta nahi, kyunki main detached rehta hoon. Ek chill observer ki tarah."}, "9.10": {"en": "Under my watch, nature creates everything, and the world keeps turning.", "hi": "Meri nigraani mein nature sab banati hai, aur duniya ghoomti rehti hai."}, "9.11": {"en": "Some people see me in human form and dismiss me. They don't see who I really am.", "hi": "Kuch log mujhe insaani roop mein dekh ke ignore kar dete hain. Woh nahi dekhte main asli mein kaun hoon."}, "9.12": {"en": "Their hopes, actions and knowledge go to waste because they're stuck in a negative mindset.", "hi": "Unki umeedein, kaam aur gyaan sab bekaar jaata hai kyunki woh negative mindset mein phanse hain."}, "9.13": {"en": "Great souls with a divine nature worship me single-mindedly, knowing I'm the source of everything.", "hi": "Divine nature wale mahaan log ek-man se meri pooja karte hain, ye jaante hue ki main sabka source hoon."}, "9.14": {"en": "They keep singing about me, stay committed, and bow with love. Pure devotion.", "hi": "Woh mere gun gaate rehte hain, committed rehte hain, aur pyaar se jhukte hain. Shuddh bhakti."}, "9.15": {"en": "Others worship me through knowledge: as one, as many, as the whole universe.", "hi": "Kuch gyaan se meri pooja karte hain: ek roop mein, anek roop mein, poore brahmaand ke roop mein."}, "9.16": {"en": "I'm the ritual, the offering, the herb, the mantra, the fire and the act of offering. I'm all of it.", "hi": "Main ritual, offering, jadi-booti, mantra, aag aur arpan ka kaam hoon. Main sab hoon."}, "9.17": {"en": "I'm the father, mother and grandparent of the universe. I'm Om, and every sacred text.", "hi": "Main brahmaand ka pita, maata aur dada hoon. Main Om hoon, aur har pavitra granth."}, "9.18": {"en": "I'm the goal, the support, the witness, the home, the refuge and the friend. The start and end of everything.", "hi": "Main goal, sahara, saakshi, ghar, sharan aur dost hoon. Sabka shuru aur ant."}, "9.19": {"en": "I bring heat and rain. I'm life and death, what exists and what doesn't.", "hi": "Main garmi aur baarish laata hoon. Main jeevan aur maut, jo hai aur jo nahi, sab hoon."}, "9.20": {"en": "Some perform rituals to get into heaven. They get there and enjoy divine pleasures.", "hi": "Kuch log swarg jaane ke liye rituals karte hain. Woh pahunchte hain aur divya sukh enjoy karte hain."}, "9.21": {"en": "But when their good-karma balance runs out, they come back. Heaven is a holiday, not a home.", "hi": "Par jab punya ka balance khatam hota hai, woh wapas aate hain. Swarg holiday hai, ghar nahi."}, "9.22": {"en": "Those who focus only on me, I take care of. What they need, I bring. What they have, I protect.", "hi": "Jo sirf mujh pe focus karte hain, unka main dhyaan rakhta hoon. Jo chahiye woh laata hoon, jo hai woh bachata hoon."}, "9.23": {"en": "Even people who worship other gods with faith are really worshipping me, just indirectly.", "hi": "Jo dusre devtaon ki bharose se pooja karte hain, woh bhi asli mein meri hi pooja karte hain, bas indirectly."}, "9.24": {"en": "I'm the one who receives every offering. Not knowing this, people slip back.", "hi": "Har offering main hi leta hoon. Ye na jaanne se log wapas fisal jaate hain."}, "9.25": {"en": "You become what you worship. Worship the gods and you go to them. Worship me and you come to me.", "hi": "Jiski pooja karo, wahi ban jaate ho. Devtaon ki karo toh unke paas, meri karo toh mere paas."}, "9.26": {"en": "A leaf, a flower, a fruit, or some water, given with love: I accept it. It's the heart that counts.", "hi": "Ek patta, phool, phal ya thoda paani, pyaar se diya: main sweekar karta hoon. Dil matter karta hai."}, "9.27": {"en": "Whatever you do, eat, give or practise, offer it to me. Turn your whole life into an offering.", "hi": "Jo bhi karo, khao, do ya practice karo, mujhe arpan karo. Poori life ko offering bana do."}, "9.28": {"en": "Do this and you're freed from good and bad karma alike. Free, you'll come to me.", "hi": "Aisa karo toh achhe-bure dono karma se free ho jaoge. Free hokar mere paas aaoge."}, "9.29": {"en": "I'm the same to everyone. No favourites, no haters. But those who love me live in me, and I in them.", "hi": "Main sabke liye same hoon. Na favourite, na dushman. Par jo mujhe pyaar karte hain, woh mujh mein, main un mein."}, "9.30": {"en": "Even someone who's done terrible things, if they turn to me sincerely, should be seen as good. They've chosen right.", "hi": "Jisne bahut galat kiya ho, agar woh dil se meri taraf mude, toh use achha maano. Usne sahi chuna hai."}, "9.31": {"en": "They change quickly and find lasting peace. Tell the world: my devotee never falls.", "hi": "Woh jaldi badalte hain aur lasting peace paate hain. Duniya ko batao: mera bhakt kabhi nahi girta."}, "9.32": {"en": "Anyone, regardless of birth, gender or class, who turns to me reaches the highest. No exceptions.", "hi": "Koi bhi, janam, gender ya class kuch bhi ho, jo meri sharan aata hai, sabse ooncha paata hai. Koi exception nahi."}, "9.33": {"en": "This world is temporary and full of struggle. So while you're here, connect with me.", "hi": "Ye duniya temporary aur struggle bhari hai. Toh jab tak yahan ho, mujhse judo."}, "9.34": {"en": "Keep your mind on me, love me, honour me, bow to me. Make me your goal and you'll reach me.", "hi": "Mind mujh pe rakho, mujhe pyaar karo, izzat do, jhuko. Mujhe goal banao, mujh tak pahunchoge."}, "10.1": {"en": "Krishna: \"Listen again, because I want what's best for you, and you love me.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Phir se suno, kyunki main tumhara bhala chahta hoon, aur tum mujhe pyaar karte ho.\""}, "10.2": {"en": "Not even gods or great sages know where I come from. I'm their source.", "hi": "Devta aur bade rishi bhi nahi jaante main kahan se aaya. Main hi unka source hoon."}, "10.3": {"en": "Whoever knows I'm unborn and beginningless, the Lord of all, is free from confusion and wrongdoing.", "hi": "Jo jaanta hai ki main ajanma, anaadi aur sabka Bhagwan hoon, woh confusion aur galti se free hai."}, "10.4": {"en": "Intelligence, wisdom, patience, truth, self-control, joy, pain, fear, courage: every quality comes from me.", "hi": "Buddhi, gyaan, sabr, sach, self-control, khushi, dard, darr, himmat: har gun mujhse aata hai."}, "10.5": {"en": "Kindness, contentment, discipline, generosity, fame and even bad reputation all arise from me.", "hi": "Dayaluta, santosh, tapasya, daan, naam aur badnaami bhi, sab mujhse paida hote hain."}, "10.6": {"en": "The great sages and the first ancestors of humanity were born from my mind.", "hi": "Mahaan rishi aur insaaniyat ke pehle purvaj mere mann se paida hue."}, "10.7": {"en": "Truly understand my glory and power, and your devotion becomes unshakeable.", "hi": "Meri mahima aur shakti sach mein samajh lo, toh tumhari bhakti atal ho jaati hai."}, "10.8": {"en": "I'm the source of everything. The wise get this and love me with their whole heart.", "hi": "Main sabka source hoon. Gyaani ye samajhte hain aur poore dil se mujhe pyaar karte hain."}, "10.9": {"en": "Their minds on me, lives centred on me, they inspire each other and talk about me. They're always happy.", "hi": "Unka mind mujh pe, life mujh pe centred, ek dusre ko inspire karte hain aur meri baatein karte hain. Hamesha khush."}, "10.10": {"en": "To those who love me constantly, I give the understanding that brings them to me.", "hi": "Jo mujhe lagataar pyaar karte hain, unhe main woh samajh deta hoon jo unhe mujh tak laati hai."}, "10.11": {"en": "Out of love, I light up their hearts and destroy the darkness of ignorance.", "hi": "Pyaar se main unke dil mein roshni karta hoon aur agyaan ka andhera mita deta hoon."}, "10.12": {"en": "Arjuna: \"You're the supreme reality, the highest light, the purest of all. The sages agree.\"", "hi": "Arjun: \"Aap param satya ho, sabse oonchi roshni, sabse pavitra. Rishi bhi yahi kehte hain.\""}, "10.13": {"en": "\"Great seers like Narada and Vyasa said so, and now you're telling me yourself.\"", "hi": "\"Narad aur Vyas jaise rishiyon ne yahi kaha, aur ab aap khud bata rahe ho.\""}, "10.14": {"en": "\"I believe everything you've said. Neither gods nor demons truly know you.\"", "hi": "\"Aapne jo kaha, mujhe sab sach lagta hai. Na devta na asur aapko sach mein jaante hain.\""}, "10.15": {"en": "\"Only you know yourself, Krishna. Creator of all, God of gods.\"", "hi": "\"Sirf aap khud ko jaante ho, Krishna. Sabke rachne wale, devon ke dev.\""}, "10.16": {"en": "\"Please tell me all the ways you show up in the world.\"", "hi": "\"Please batao aap duniya mein kin-kin roop mein ho.\""}, "10.17": {"en": "\"How can I keep thinking of you? Where should I look to find you?\"", "hi": "\"Main aapko lagataar kaise yaad karun? Aapko kahan dhoondun?\""}, "10.18": {"en": "\"Tell me again in detail. I can't get enough of hearing you.\" Arjuna is hooked.", "hi": "\"Phir se detail mein batao. Aapko sunte hue mann nahi bharta.\" Arjun hooked hai."}, "10.19": {"en": "Krishna: \"I'll share the highlights. My glories are literally endless.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Main highlights batata hoon. Meri mahima ka koi ant nahi.\""}, "10.20": {"en": "I'm the self inside every heart. The beginning, middle and end of every being.", "hi": "Main har dil ke andar ka self hoon. Har jeev ka shuru, beech aur ant."}, "10.21": {"en": "Among lights I'm the sun, among night skies I'm the moon. Wherever something shines brightest, that's me.", "hi": "Roshniyon mein main suraj, raat ke aasmaan mein chaand. Jo sabse zyada chamakta hai, woh main hoon."}, "10.22": {"en": "Among scriptures I'm the musical Sama Veda, among senses I'm the mind, in living beings I'm consciousness.", "hi": "Granthon mein main sangeet wala Saam Veda, senses mein mind, aur jeevon mein chetna hoon."}, "10.23": {"en": "Among Rudras I'm Shiva, among mountains I'm Meru. The best of every category is me.", "hi": "Rudron mein main Shiv, pahadon mein Meru. Har category ka best main hoon."}, "10.24": {"en": "Among priests I'm Brihaspati, among generals Skanda, among waters the ocean.", "hi": "Purohiton mein main Brihaspati, senapatiyon mein Skand, jal mein samundar."}, "10.25": {"en": "Among words I'm Om, among prayers I'm quiet chanting, among the unmoving I'm the Himalayas.", "hi": "Shabdon mein main Om, prarthanaon mein jap, sthir cheezon mein Himalaya."}, "10.26": {"en": "Among trees I'm the sacred fig, among divine sages Narada, among perfected beings Kapila.", "hi": "Pedon mein main peepal, devrishiyon mein Narad, siddhon mein Kapil."}, "10.27": {"en": "Among horses I'm the divine Uchchaihshravas, among elephants Airavata, among people the leader.", "hi": "Ghodon mein main Uchchaishrava, haathiyon mein Airavat, insaanon mein raja."}, "10.28": {"en": "Among weapons I'm the thunderbolt, among cows the wish-fulfilling one, among serpents Vasuki.", "hi": "Hathiyaron mein main vajra, gaayon mein Kamdhenu, saanpon mein Vasuki."}, "10.29": {"en": "Among snakes I'm Ananta, among water beings Varuna, among those who keep order, Yama.", "hi": "Naagon mein main Anant, jal jeevon mein Varun, niyam rakhne walon mein Yamraj."}, "10.30": {"en": "Among animals I'm the lion, among birds Garuda, among demons' kids the devoted Prahlada.", "hi": "Jaanwaron mein main sher, pakshiyon mein Garud, daityon mein bhakt Prahlad."}, "10.31": {"en": "Among moving things I'm the wind, among warriors Rama, among rivers the Ganga.", "hi": "Chalne wali cheezon mein main hawa, yoddhaon mein Ram, nadiyon mein Ganga."}, "10.32": {"en": "I'm the start, middle and end of creation. Among sciences, self-knowledge. In a debate, honest logic.", "hi": "Main srishti ka shuru, beech aur ant hoon. Vidyaon mein aatma-gyaan. Bahas mein sachcha tark."}, "10.33": {"en": "Among letters I'm 'A'. I'm endless time itself, and the creator who sees in every direction.", "hi": "Aksharon mein main 'A' hoon. Main anant samay hoon, aur har disha dekhne wala rachnakar."}, "10.34": {"en": "I'm death that takes all, and the source of all that's coming. I'm fame, memory, patience and forgiveness.", "hi": "Main sab le jaane wali maut hoon, aur aane wale sabka source. Main yash, smriti, dhairya aur kshama hoon."}, "10.35": {"en": "Among hymns I'm the Brihat Saman, among metres the Gayatri, among seasons spring.", "hi": "Stotron mein main Brihat Saam, chhandon mein Gayatri, ritu mein basant."}, "10.36": {"en": "I'm the brilliance of the brilliant, the victory, the effort, and the goodness of good people.", "hi": "Main talented ki chamak, jeet, mehnat, aur achhe logon ki achhai hoon."}, "10.37": {"en": "Among the Vrishnis I'm Krishna, among the Pandavas Arjuna, among sages Vyasa. Yes, Arjuna, you too.", "hi": "Vrishniyon mein main Krishna, Pandavon mein Arjun, muniyon mein Vyas. Haan Arjun, tum bhi."}, "10.38": {"en": "I'm discipline among rulers, strategy among winners, silence among secrets, wisdom among the wise.", "hi": "Main shaasakon ka anushasan, jeetne walon ki neeti, raazon mein maun, aur gyaaniyon ka gyaan hoon."}, "10.39": {"en": "I'm the seed of every being. Nothing moving or still exists without me.", "hi": "Main har jeev ka beej hoon. Chalta ya ruka, kuch bhi mere bina nahi."}, "10.40": {"en": "My divine forms have no limit. This was just a small sample.", "hi": "Mere divya roopon ki koi seema nahi. Ye bas chhota sa sample tha."}, "10.41": {"en": "Wherever you see power, beauty or greatness, that's a tiny spark of me.", "hi": "Jahan bhi taakat, sundarta ya mahaanta dikhe, woh meri ek chhoti si chingari hai."}, "10.42": {"en": "But why all these details? Just know: I hold up this entire universe with a tiny fraction of myself.", "hi": "Par itni detail kyun? Bas jaan lo: main poore brahmaand ko apne ek chhote se hisse se sambhale hoon."}, "11.1": {"en": "Arjuna: \"You've shared the deepest secret with me, and my confusion is gone.\"", "hi": "Arjun: \"Aapne mujhe sabse gehra raaz bataya, aur mera confusion chala gaya.\""}, "11.2": {"en": "\"I've heard how everything begins and ends in you, and how great you are.\"", "hi": "\"Maine suna ki sab kuch aap mein shuru aur khatam hota hai, aur aap kitne mahaan ho.\""}, "11.3": {"en": "\"I believe you. But now I want to actually see your divine form.\"", "hi": "\"Mujhe aap pe bharosa hai. Par ab main aapka divya roop sach mein dekhna chahta hoon.\""}, "11.4": {"en": "\"If you think I can handle it, please show me.\" Brave request.", "hi": "\"Agar aapko lagta hai main handle kar sakta hoon, toh please dikhao.\" Bahaduri wali request."}, "11.5": {"en": "Krishna: \"Then look. Hundreds and thousands of my forms, in every colour and shape.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Toh dekho. Mere sainkdon-hazaaron roop, har rang aur shape mein.\""}, "11.6": {"en": "\"See all the gods and wonders no one has ever seen before.\"", "hi": "\"Saare devta aur woh ajoobe dekho jo kisi ne pehle nahi dekhe.\""}, "11.7": {"en": "\"The whole universe, everything moving and still, is right here in my body. Look.\"", "hi": "\"Poora brahmaand, har chalti aur ruki cheez, yahin mere shareer mein hai. Dekho.\""}, "11.8": {"en": "\"Your normal eyes can't handle this. Here, I'm giving you divine vision.\" Upgrade unlocked.", "hi": "\"Tumhari normal aankhein ye nahi dekh sakti. Lo, main tumhe divya drishti deta hoon.\" Upgrade unlocked."}, "11.9": {"en": "And then Krishna reveals his supreme cosmic form. The biggest reveal in the Gita.", "hi": "Aur phir Krishna apna param vishwaroop dikhate hain. Gita ka sabse bada reveal."}, "11.10": {"en": "Countless faces and eyes, endless wonders, divine jewellery and weapons everywhere.", "hi": "Anginat chehre aur aankhein, anant ajoobe, har taraf divya gehne aur hathiyar."}, "11.11": {"en": "Divine garlands and robes, heavenly fragrance, glowing, infinite, facing every direction at once.", "hi": "Divya maalaayein aur vastra, swargiya khushboo, chamakta hua, anant, ek saath har disha mein."}, "11.12": {"en": "Imagine a thousand suns rising at once. That's how bright this form was.", "hi": "Socho ek saath hazaar suraj ug jaayein. Itna tez tha ye roop."}, "11.13": {"en": "Arjuna saw the entire universe, in all its variety, in one place: inside Krishna.", "hi": "Arjun ne poora brahmaand, apni har variety ke saath, ek jagah dekha: Krishna ke andar."}, "11.14": {"en": "Arjuna is stunned, goosebumps everywhere. He bows his head and folds his hands.", "hi": "Arjun hairaan hai, rongte khade. Sar jhukata hai aur haath jodta hai."}, "11.15": {"en": "\"I see all the gods, all beings, Brahma, the sages and the divine serpents in you.\"", "hi": "\"Mujhe aap mein saare devta, saare jeev, Brahma, rishi aur divya naag dikh rahe hain.\""}, "11.16": {"en": "\"Endless arms, faces and eyes everywhere. I can't find your beginning, middle or end.\"", "hi": "\"Har taraf anginat haath, chehre aur aankhein. Aapka shuru, beech ya ant nahi dikhta.\""}, "11.17": {"en": "\"You're a mass of blazing light, like fire and the sun. Hard to even look at.\"", "hi": "\"Aap jalti roshni ka dher ho, aag aur suraj jaise. Dekhna bhi mushkil hai.\""}, "11.18": {"en": "\"You're the eternal, the highest truth, the support of everything, the protector of what's right.\"", "hi": "\"Aap amar ho, param satya, sabka aadhaar, dharm ke rakshak.\""}, "11.19": {"en": "\"No beginning, no end, infinite power. Sun and moon are your eyes. Your fire heats the universe.\"", "hi": "\"Na shuru, na ant, anant shakti. Suraj aur chaand aapki aankhein. Aapki aag brahmaand ko tapati hai.\""}, "11.20": {"en": "\"You fill the space between earth and sky. All three worlds are shaking at this sight.\"", "hi": "\"Aap dharti aur aakash ke beech sab bhar dete ho. Teenon lok ye dekh ke kaanp rahe hain.\""}, "11.21": {"en": "\"Gods are entering you. Some, afraid, pray with folded hands. Sages sing your praises.\"", "hi": "\"Devta aap mein samaa rahe hain. Kuch darr ke haath jod rahe hain. Rishi aapke gun gaa rahe hain.\""}, "11.22": {"en": "\"Every kind of divine being is staring at you in total amazement.\"", "hi": "\"Har tarah ke divya jeev aapko poori hairaani se dekh rahe hain.\""}, "11.23": {"en": "\"So many mouths, eyes, arms and terrifying teeth. The worlds are trembling, and so am I.\"", "hi": "\"Itne munh, aankhein, haath aur darawne daant. Duniya kaanp rahi hai, aur main bhi.\""}, "11.24": {"en": "\"You're touching the sky, blazing in every colour. I'm shaking inside and can't find calm.\"", "hi": "\"Aap aasmaan chhoo rahe ho, har rang mein chamak rahe ho. Main andar se kaanp raha hoon, shaanti nahi mil rahi.\""}, "11.25": {"en": "\"Your mouths look like the fire at the end of time. I'm lost. Please, have mercy.\"", "hi": "\"Aapke munh pralay ki aag jaise lagte hain. Main kho gaya hoon. Please, daya karo.\""}, "11.26": {"en": "\"I see Duryodhana's brothers, Bhishma, Drona, Karna, and our warriors too...\"", "hi": "\"Mujhe Duryodhan ke bhai, Bheeshma, Drona, Karna, aur hamare yoddha bhi dikh rahe hain...\""}, "11.27": {"en": "\"...rushing into your terrifying mouths and being crushed.\" Arjuna sees the outcome before the battle.", "hi": "\"...aapke darawne munh mein ghuste aur pis-te hue.\" Arjun ladai se pehle hi result dekh leta hai."}, "11.28": {"en": "\"Like rivers rushing into the ocean, these heroes are flowing into your blazing mouths.\"", "hi": "\"Jaise nadiyaan samundar mein bhaagti hain, ye veer aapke jalte munh mein beh rahe hain.\""}, "11.29": {"en": "\"Like moths flying into a flame, they're rushing to their end.\"", "hi": "\"Jaise patange aag mein udte hain, waise ye apne ant ki taraf bhaag rahe hain.\""}, "11.30": {"en": "\"You're swallowing the worlds with your flaming mouths. Your rays are burning up the universe.\"", "hi": "\"Aap apne jalte munh se duniya nigal rahe ho. Aapki kiranein brahmaand ko jala rahi hain.\""}, "11.31": {"en": "\"Who are you in this terrifying form? Please be kind. I want to understand you.\"", "hi": "\"Is darawne roop mein aap kaun ho? Please daya karo. Main aapko samajhna chahta hoon.\""}, "11.32": {"en": "Krishna: \"I am Time, the destroyer of worlds. Even without you, these warriors won't survive.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Main Kaal hoon, duniya ka naash karne wala. Tumhare bina bhi ye yoddha nahi bachenge.\""}, "11.33": {"en": "\"So rise and win. I've already decided the outcome. You're just the instrument.\"", "hi": "\"Toh utho aur jeeto. Result maine pehle hi tay kar diya hai. Tum bas nimitt ho.\""}, "11.34": {"en": "\"Their fate is sealed. Don't be distressed. Fight, and you'll win.\"", "hi": "\"Unka bhagya tay hai. Pareshaan mat ho. Lado, aur tum jeetoge.\""}, "11.35": {"en": "Arjuna, trembling and emotional, bows again and again and speaks with folded hands.", "hi": "Arjun, kaanpte aur emotional, baar-baar jhukta hai aur haath jod ke bolta hai."}, "11.36": {"en": "\"No wonder the world celebrates you. Negativity runs away, and the wise bow to you.\"", "hi": "\"Isliye duniya aapka jashn manati hai. Negativity bhaagti hai, aur gyaani aapko pranaam karte hain.\""}, "11.37": {"en": "\"Why wouldn't they bow? You're the creator of even the creator. Infinite, Lord of gods.\"", "hi": "\"Woh kyun na jhukein? Aap toh rachnakar ke bhi rachnakar ho. Anant, devon ke dev.\""}, "11.38": {"en": "\"You're the first God, the ancient one, the resting place of the universe, the knower and the known.\"", "hi": "\"Aap pehle Bhagwan ho, sabse purane, brahmaand ka vishraam, jaanne wale aur jaanne layak bhi.\""}, "11.39": {"en": "\"You're wind, fire, water, the moon, the creator. A thousand salutes to you, again and again.\"", "hi": "\"Aap hawa, aag, paani, chaand, rachnakar ho. Aapko hazaar baar pranaam, baar baar.\""}, "11.40": {"en": "\"Salutes from the front, from behind, from every side. You're everything, infinite in power.\"", "hi": "\"Aage se, peeche se, har taraf se pranaam. Aap sab kuch ho, anant shakti wale.\""}, "11.41": {"en": "\"I called you 'buddy' and 'Krishna' casually, not knowing who you really are...\"", "hi": "\"Maine aapko casually 'yaar' aur 'Krishna' bulaya, ye jaane bina ki aap asli mein kaun ho...\""}, "11.42": {"en": "\"...and joked around with you while eating and hanging out. Please forgive me.\" Best friend realising his friend is God.", "hi": "\"...aur khaate-peete, ghoomte hue mazaak kiya. Please maaf karo.\" Best friend ko pata chala dost Bhagwan hai."}, "11.43": {"en": "\"You're the father of the world, the greatest teacher. No one equals you, let alone surpasses you.\"", "hi": "\"Aap duniya ke pita ho, sabse bade guru. Koi aapke barabar nahi, aage toh door ki baat.\""}, "11.44": {"en": "\"I bow down completely. Forgive me like a father forgives a son, a friend a friend.\"", "hi": "\"Main poori tarah jhukta hoon. Maaf karo jaise pita bete ko, dost dost ko karta hai.\""}, "11.45": {"en": "\"I'm thrilled but also scared. Please show me your familiar form again.\"", "hi": "\"Main khush bhi hoon aur darr bhi raha hoon. Please apna jaana-pehchana roop phir dikhao.\""}, "11.46": {"en": "\"I want to see you with your crown, mace and discus, in your four-armed form.\"", "hi": "\"Main aapko mukut, gada aur chakra ke saath, chaturbhuj roop mein dekhna chahta hoon.\""}, "11.47": {"en": "Krishna: \"Out of love I showed you this form. No one but you has ever seen it.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Pyaar se maine tumhe ye roop dikhaya. Tumhare siva kisi ne ise nahi dekha.\""}, "11.48": {"en": "\"Not scriptures, rituals, charity or hard discipline can show this form. Only grace.\"", "hi": "\"Na granth, na rituals, na daan, na tapasya ye roop dikha sakte hain. Sirf kripa.\""}, "11.49": {"en": "\"Don't be scared or confused. Relax, and look at my familiar form again.\"", "hi": "\"Daro mat, confuse mat ho. Relax karo, aur mera jaana-pehchana roop phir dekho.\""}, "11.50": {"en": "Krishna returns to his gentle human form and comforts the shaken Arjuna.", "hi": "Krishna apne saumya insaani roop mein lautte hain aur hile hue Arjun ko sambhalte hain."}, "11.51": {"en": "Arjuna: \"Seeing your human form again, I feel calm and like myself.\"", "hi": "Arjun: \"Aapka insaani roop phir dekh ke main shaant hoon aur normal feel kar raha hoon.\""}, "11.52": {"en": "\"Even the gods long to see the form you just saw. It's incredibly rare.\"", "hi": "\"Jo roop tumne dekha, use dekhne ko devta bhi tarasate hain. Bahut rare hai.\""}, "11.53": {"en": "\"Not through study, discipline, charity or rituals can anyone see me like that.\"", "hi": "\"Padhai, tapasya, daan ya rituals se koi mujhe aise nahi dekh sakta.\""}, "11.54": {"en": "\"Only through pure, single-minded love can someone truly know, see and become one with me.\"", "hi": "\"Sirf shuddh, ek-man pyaar se koi mujhe sach mein jaan, dekh aur mujhse ek ho sakta hai.\""}, "11.55": {"en": "Work for me, make me your goal, love me, drop attachments and hate no one. That's how you reach me.", "hi": "Mere liye kaam karo, mujhe goal banao, pyaar karo, attachment chhodo, kisi se nafrat mat karo. Aise mujh tak pahunchoge."}, "12.1": {"en": "Arjuna: \"Who's doing it better, those who love you in a personal form or those who meditate on the formless?\"", "hi": "Arjun: \"Kaun better hai, jo aapke saakar roop ko pyaar karte hain ya jo niraakar ka dhyaan karte hain?\""}, "12.2": {"en": "Krishna: \"Those who focus on me with full faith and love, I consider the best.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Jo poore bharose aur pyaar se mujh pe focus karte hain, unhe main best maanta hoon.\""}, "12.3": {"en": "\"Those who meditate on the formless, infinite and unchanging...\"", "hi": "\"Jo niraakar, anant aur kabhi na badalne wale ka dhyaan karte hain...\""}, "12.4": {"en": "\"...with self-control, balance and care for everyone, also reach me.\"", "hi": "\"...self-control, balance aur sabki parwaah ke saath, woh bhi mujh tak pahunchte hain.\""}, "12.5": {"en": "But the formless path is much harder. It's tough for humans to connect with something abstract.", "hi": "Par niraakar ka raasta bahut mushkil hai. Insaan ke liye abstract cheez se judna tough hai."}, "12.6": {"en": "Those who dedicate everything to me, make me their goal and meditate on me with love...", "hi": "Jo sab kuch mujhe arpan karte hain, mujhe goal banate hain aur pyaar se mera dhyaan karte hain..."}, "12.7": {"en": "...I quickly pull them out of the ocean of struggle. I've got them.", "hi": "...unhe main jaldi sansaar ke samundar se nikaal leta hoon. Main hoon unke saath."}, "12.8": {"en": "Keep your mind and thoughts on me, and you'll live in me. No doubt.", "hi": "Mind aur soch mujh pe rakho, aur tum mujh mein rahoge. Koi shak nahi."}, "12.9": {"en": "Can't focus on me constantly? Then practise. Bring your mind back, again and again.", "hi": "Lagataar focus nahi hota? Toh practice karo. Mind ko baar-baar wapas lao."}, "12.10": {"en": "Can't practise regularly? Then just do your work for me. That alone gets you there.", "hi": "Regular practice nahi hoti? Toh bas mere liye kaam karo. Usi se pahunch jaoge."}, "12.11": {"en": "Can't even do that? Then just let go of the results of what you do. Start there.", "hi": "Woh bhi nahi hota? Toh bas apne kaam ke result chhod do. Wahin se shuru karo."}, "12.12": {"en": "Understanding beats mechanical practice, meditation beats understanding, and letting go of results brings instant peace.", "hi": "Samajh mechanical practice se better, dhyaan samajh se better, aur result chhodna turant shaanti deta hai."}, "12.13": {"en": "No hate, always kind, no ego, calm through ups and downs, forgiving. That person is dear to me.", "hi": "Na nafrat, hamesha dayalu, na ego, ups-downs mein shaant, maaf karne wala. Aisa insaan mujhe pyaara hai."}, "12.14": {"en": "Content, disciplined, determined, mind and heart given to me. That person is dear to me.", "hi": "Santusht, disciplined, determined, mind aur dil mujhe diya hua. Aisa insaan mujhe pyaara hai."}, "12.15": {"en": "They don't disturb anyone, and no one disturbs them. Free from excitement, fear and stress. Dear to me.", "hi": "Na woh kisi ko pareshaan karte, na koi unhe. Excitement, darr aur stress se free. Mujhe pyaare."}, "12.16": {"en": "No neediness, clean inside, skilled, unbothered, not chasing every new project. Dear to me.", "hi": "Na needy, andar se saaf, skilled, unbothered, har naye project ke peeche nahi bhaagte. Mujhe pyaare."}, "12.17": {"en": "Not overly happy, hateful, sad or greedy. Beyond good and bad, full of love for me. Dear to me.", "hi": "Na zyada khush, na nafrat, na udaas, na laalach. Achhe-bure se pare, mere pyaar se bhare. Mujhe pyaare."}, "12.18": {"en": "Same with friends and enemies, respect and insult, heat and cold, pleasure and pain. No attachments.", "hi": "Dost-dushman, izzat-beizzati, garmi-sardi, sukh-dukh, sabme same. Koi attachment nahi."}, "12.19": {"en": "Praise or criticism, same reaction. Speaks less, content with whatever, steady and devoted. Dear to me.", "hi": "Taareef ho ya burai, same reaction. Kam bolta hai, jo mile usme khush, steady aur bhakt. Mujhe pyaara."}, "12.20": {"en": "Those who live these values with faith and make me their goal are the dearest of all to me.", "hi": "Jo in values ko bharose se jeete hain aur mujhe goal banate hain, woh mujhe sabse zyada pyaare hain."}, "13.1": {"en": "Arjuna wants to understand the basics: the body, the soul, and how knowing really works.", "hi": "Arjun basics samajhna chahta hai: body, aatma, aur gyaan asli mein kaise kaam karta hai."}, "13.2": {"en": "Krishna: \"Your body is the field. The one who knows the body is the knower of the field.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Tumhara body khet hai. Jo body ko jaanta hai, woh khet ka jaankaar hai.\""}, "13.3": {"en": "\"I'm the knower in every body. Understanding the body and the knower is real knowledge.\"", "hi": "\"Har body mein jaanne wala main hoon. Body aur jaanne wale ko samajhna hi asli gyaan hai.\""}, "13.4": {"en": "\"Let me quickly explain what the body is, how it changes, and who the self is.\"", "hi": "\"Chalo jaldi samjhata hoon ki body kya hai, kaise badalti hai, aur self kaun hai.\""}, "13.5": {"en": "Sages have explained this in many ways, through hymns and solid logic.", "hi": "Rishiyon ne ye kai tareekon se samjhaya hai, bhajanon aur pakke tark se."}, "13.6": {"en": "The elements, ego, intellect, the senses and what they experience. That's the field.", "hi": "Tatva, ego, buddhi, senses aur jo woh experience karte hain. Yahi khet hai."}, "13.7": {"en": "Desire, hate, pleasure, pain and awareness are all part of the field, too.", "hi": "Chahat, nafrat, sukh, dukh aur chetna, ye sab bhi khet ka hissa hain."}, "13.8": {"en": "Real wisdom looks like humility, no showing off, non-violence, patience, honesty and respect for teachers.", "hi": "Asli gyaan aisa dikhta hai: vinamrata, dikhawa nahi, ahimsa, sabr, imaandaari aur guru ki izzat."}, "13.9": {"en": "Not chasing sense pleasures, no ego, and seeing clearly that birth, ageing and illness bring pain.", "hi": "Sense ke mazon ke peeche na bhaagna, ego nahi, aur saaf dekhna ki janam, budhapa aur bimaari dukh laate hain."}, "13.10": {"en": "Not clinging to people and stuff, and staying balanced whether things go your way or not.", "hi": "Logon aur cheezon se na chipakna, aur cheezein apne hisaab se hon ya na hon, balance rakhna."}, "13.11": {"en": "Steady devotion, enjoying solitude, and not needing the crowd's approval.", "hi": "Pakki bhakti, akelapan enjoy karna, aur bheed ki approval na chahiye hona."}, "13.12": {"en": "Keep reflecting on who you really are and searching for truth. That's wisdom. The rest is ignorance.", "hi": "Lagataar socho tum asli mein kaun ho aur sach dhoondo. Yahi gyaan hai. Baaki agyaan hai."}, "13.13": {"en": "Now, what's worth knowing: the eternal truth. Know it and you become immortal.", "hi": "Ab, jo jaanne layak hai: shaashvat sach. Ise jaano toh amar ho jaate ho."}, "13.14": {"en": "It has hands, feet, eyes and ears everywhere. It covers everything.", "hi": "Iske haath, pair, aankhein aur kaan har jagah hain. Ye sab ko dhake hai."}, "13.15": {"en": "It powers the senses without having senses. It supports all but clings to nothing.", "hi": "Ye senses ko chalata hai bina khud senses ke. Sabko sambhalta hai par kisi se chipakta nahi."}, "13.16": {"en": "It's inside and outside everything, still yet moving, far away yet really close.", "hi": "Ye har cheez ke andar aur bahar hai, ruka hua par chalta, door par bilkul paas."}, "13.17": {"en": "It's one, but seems divided among beings. It creates, sustains and absorbs everything.", "hi": "Ye ek hai, par jeevon mein bata hua lagta hai. Ye sab banata, sambhalta aur samet leta hai."}, "13.18": {"en": "It's the light behind all lights, beyond darkness, and it lives in every heart.", "hi": "Ye har roshni ke peeche ki roshni hai, andhere se pare, aur har dil mein rehti hai."}, "13.19": {"en": "That's the field, wisdom and the truth, in short. Understand it and you're ready for me.", "hi": "Short mein yahi khet, gyaan aur sach hai. Ise samjho toh tum mere liye ready ho."}, "13.20": {"en": "Nature and the soul both have no beginning. All changes and qualities come from nature.", "hi": "Prakriti aur aatma dono anaadi hain. Saare badlaav aur gun prakriti se aate hain."}, "13.21": {"en": "Nature does the doing. The soul is what experiences pleasure and pain.", "hi": "Karne ka kaam prakriti karti hai. Sukh-dukh ka anubhav aatma karti hai."}, "13.22": {"en": "The soul gets attached to nature's qualities, and that attachment decides the next birth.", "hi": "Aatma prakriti ke gunon se jud jaati hai, aur yahi attachment agla janam tay karta hai."}, "13.23": {"en": "The soul in you is the witness, the supporter, the experiencer, the supreme self.", "hi": "Tumhare andar ki aatma saakshi, sahara, anubhav karne wali, param aatma hai."}, "13.24": {"en": "Understand the soul and nature properly, and you won't be reborn, whatever your situation.", "hi": "Aatma aur prakriti ko theek se samjho, toh dobara janam nahi hoga, chahe tumhari situation kuch bhi ho."}, "13.25": {"en": "Some find the self through meditation, some through knowledge, some through selfless work.", "hi": "Koi self ko dhyaan se paata hai, koi gyaan se, koi selfless kaam se."}, "13.26": {"en": "Others just listen to the wise and follow with faith. They get there too.", "hi": "Kuch log bas gyaaniyon ko sunte hain aur bharose se follow karte hain. Woh bhi pahunchte hain."}, "13.27": {"en": "Everything that's born, moving or still, comes from body and soul coming together.", "hi": "Jo bhi paida hota hai, chalta ya ruka, body aur aatma ke milne se hota hai."}, "13.28": {"en": "Whoever sees the same eternal divine in every being, even as bodies die, truly sees.", "hi": "Jo har jeev mein ek hi amar divine dekhta hai, body marne ke baad bhi, wahi sach mein dekhta hai."}, "13.29": {"en": "Seeing the divine equally everywhere, you stop hurting yourself and reach the highest.", "hi": "Har jagah barabar divine dekhne se tum khud ko hurt karna band karte ho aur sabse ooncha paate ho."}, "13.30": {"en": "Whoever sees that nature does the acting, not the soul, truly sees.", "hi": "Jo dekhta hai ki karm prakriti karti hai, aatma nahi, wahi sach mein dekhta hai."}, "13.31": {"en": "When you see all the variety coming from one source, you've found the ultimate.", "hi": "Jab saari variety ek hi source se aati dikhe, tab tumne ultimate paa liya."}, "13.32": {"en": "The supreme self lives in the body but never changes, never acts and is never stained.", "hi": "Param aatma body mein rehti hai par kabhi badalti nahi, karti nahi, aur daag nahi lagta."}, "13.33": {"en": "Like space is everywhere but nothing sticks to it, the soul isn't stained by the body.", "hi": "Jaise aakash har jagah hai par us pe kuch chipakta nahi, waise aatma body se maili nahi hoti."}, "13.34": {"en": "Like one sun lights up the whole world, the soul lights up the whole body.", "hi": "Jaise ek suraj poori duniya ko roshan karta hai, waise aatma poore body ko."}, "13.35": {"en": "See the difference between body and soul clearly, and how to break free, and you reach the supreme.", "hi": "Body aur aatma ka farak saaf dekho, aur free hone ka tareeka, toh param tak pahunchoge."}, "14.1": {"en": "Krishna: \"Here's the highest knowledge again. Sages who knew this reached perfection.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Ye raha sabse ooncha gyaan phir se. Jo rishi ise jaante the, woh perfection tak pahunche.\""}, "14.2": {"en": "Those who get this become like me. They're not reborn or shaken at the end of the world.", "hi": "Jo ye samajhte hain, woh mere jaise ho jaate hain. Na dobara janam, na pralay mein hilte hain."}, "14.3": {"en": "Nature is like the womb of the universe, and I plant the seed. That's how all life begins.", "hi": "Prakriti brahmaand ki kokh jaisi hai, aur beej main daalta hoon. Aise sab jeevan shuru hota hai."}, "14.4": {"en": "Every life form comes from nature as the mother, and I'm the father.", "hi": "Har jeev prakriti maa se aata hai, aur pita main hoon."}, "14.5": {"en": "Three energies, goodness, passion and inertia, keep the soul tied to the body.", "hi": "Teen energies, sattva, rajas aur tamas, aatma ko body se baandhe rakhti hain."}, "14.6": {"en": "Goodness is clean and bright, but even it can trap you through attachment to happiness and knowledge.", "hi": "Sattva saaf aur roshan hai, par woh bhi khushi aur gyaan ke attachment se phansa sakta hai."}, "14.7": {"en": "Passion comes from craving and attachment, and it hooks you on constant activity. Hustle-culture energy.", "hi": "Rajas craving aur attachment se aata hai, aur tumhe lagataar kaam ka addict banata hai. Hustle culture energy."}, "14.8": {"en": "Inertia comes from ignorance and traps you with laziness, carelessness and too much sleep.", "hi": "Tamas agyaan se aata hai aur aalas, laparwahi aur zyada neend se phansata hai."}, "14.9": {"en": "Goodness chains you to happiness, passion to work, and inertia to carelessness.", "hi": "Sattva khushi se baandhta hai, rajas kaam se, aur tamas laparwahi se."}, "14.10": {"en": "These three compete constantly. Sometimes one wins, sometimes another. Your mood is the scoreboard.", "hi": "Ye teeno lagataar compete karte hain. Kabhi ek jeetta hai, kabhi dusra. Tumhara mood scoreboard hai."}, "14.11": {"en": "When clarity and understanding shine through all your senses, goodness is in charge.", "hi": "Jab har sense se clarity aur samajh chamke, tab sattva in charge hai."}, "14.12": {"en": "Greed, restlessness, taking on too much and constant craving: that's passion in charge.", "hi": "Laalach, bechaini, zyada kaam utha lena aur lagataar craving: ye rajas in charge hai."}, "14.13": {"en": "Darkness, laziness, carelessness and confusion: that's inertia in charge.", "hi": "Andhera, aalas, laparwahi aur confusion: ye tamas in charge hai."}, "14.14": {"en": "Leave the world in a state of goodness and you go to the higher, purer realms.", "hi": "Sattva ki halat mein duniya chhodo toh oonche, shuddh lokon mein jaate ho."}, "14.15": {"en": "Leave in passion and you're born among workaholics. Leave in inertia and you're born into dullness.", "hi": "Rajas mein jaao toh workaholics mein janam. Tamas mein jaao toh susti bhari jagah janam."}, "14.16": {"en": "Good deeds lead to purity, passion leads to pain, and inertia leads to ignorance.", "hi": "Achhe karm se shuddhta, rajas se dukh, aur tamas se agyaan milta hai."}, "14.17": {"en": "Goodness brings wisdom, passion brings greed, inertia brings carelessness and confusion.", "hi": "Sattva gyaan laata hai, rajas laalach, tamas laparwahi aur confusion."}, "14.18": {"en": "Live in goodness and you rise. Live in passion and you stay stuck. Live in inertia and you sink.", "hi": "Sattva mein jiyo toh upar uthte ho. Rajas mein toh wahin atke rehte ho. Tamas mein toh neeche girte ho."}, "14.19": {"en": "See that these three energies are behind every action and know what's beyond them. Then you reach me.", "hi": "Dekho ki har action ke peeche ye teen energies hain aur jaano inke pare kya hai. Tab mujh tak pahunchoge."}, "14.20": {"en": "Rise above all three and you're free from birth, death, ageing and pain.", "hi": "Teeno se upar utho toh janam, maut, budhape aur dukh se free ho jaate ho."}, "14.21": {"en": "Arjuna: \"How do I spot someone who's gone beyond all three? How do they act?\"", "hi": "Arjun: \"Jo teeno se pare chala gaya, use kaise pehchanun? Woh kaise behave karta hai?\""}, "14.22": {"en": "They don't resent clarity, busyness or confusion when it comes, and don't miss it when it goes.", "hi": "Clarity, busyness ya confusion aaye toh unse chidte nahi, aur jaaye toh miss nahi karte."}, "14.23": {"en": "They sit back like an observer. \"Oh, it's just the energies doing their thing.\" Unshaken.", "hi": "Woh observer ki tarah baithte hain. \"Arre, ye toh bas energies apna kaam kar rahi hain.\" Atal."}, "14.24": {"en": "Same in pleasure and pain. Dirt, stone and gold look the same to them. Calm with praise or blame.", "hi": "Sukh-dukh mein same. Mitti, patthar aur sona sab ek jaise. Taareef ya burai mein shaant."}, "14.25": {"en": "Same in honour and insult, with friends and enemies, not chasing ego projects. They're beyond the energies.", "hi": "Izzat-beizzati mein same, dost-dushman ke saath same, ego projects ke peeche nahi. Woh energies se pare hain."}, "14.26": {"en": "Those who love and serve me steadily rise above all three and reach the ultimate.", "hi": "Jo mujhe lagataar pyaar aur seva karte hain, woh teeno se upar uthke ultimate tak pahunchte hain."}, "14.27": {"en": "I'm the foundation of the ultimate: eternal, unchanging truth and complete bliss.", "hi": "Main ultimate ki neev hoon: amar, kabhi na badalne wala sach aur poora anand."}, "15.1": {"en": "Life is like an upside-down tree, roots in the divine, branches spreading down into the world. Understand it and you get it all.", "hi": "Zindagi ulte ped jaisi hai, jadein divine mein, shaakhaayein duniya mein neeche phaili. Ise samjho toh sab samajh aata hai."}, "15.2": {"en": "Its branches grow on our moods, its buds are sense pleasures, and its roots keep pulling us into action.", "hi": "Iski shaakhaayein hamare moods pe badhti hain, kaliyaan sense ke maze hain, aur jadein humein karm mein kheenchti hain."}, "15.3": {"en": "You can't see where it starts or ends. Cut through it with the strong axe of detachment.", "hi": "Iska shuru ya ant nahi dikhta. Detachment ki mazboot kulhaadi se ise kaat do."}, "15.4": {"en": "Then search for the place you never come back from, and take refuge in the original source.", "hi": "Phir woh jagah dhoondo jahan se wapas nahi aate, aur asli source ki sharan lo."}, "15.5": {"en": "No ego, no clinging, focused on the self, free from cravings and highs and lows. That's how you get there.", "hi": "Na ego, na chipakna, self pe focus, cravings aur ups-downs se free. Aise pahunchte ho."}, "15.6": {"en": "My home isn't lit by sun, moon or fire. Reach it and you never come back.", "hi": "Mere ghar ko suraj, chaand ya aag roshan nahi karte. Wahan pahuncho toh wapas nahi aate."}, "15.7": {"en": "Every soul is a forever part of me. In this world it gets pulled by the mind and senses.", "hi": "Har aatma mera hamesha ka hissa hai. Is duniya mein woh mind aur senses se kheenchi jaati hai."}, "15.8": {"en": "When the soul switches bodies, it carries the mind and senses along, like wind carries a scent.", "hi": "Jab aatma body badalti hai, mind aur senses saath le jaati hai, jaise hawa khushboo le jaati hai."}, "15.9": {"en": "Through ears, eyes, skin, tongue, nose and mind, the soul experiences the world.", "hi": "Kaan, aankh, twacha, jeebh, naak aur mind se aatma duniya ka anubhav karti hai."}, "15.10": {"en": "Confused people don't notice the soul coming, staying or leaving. People with insight do.", "hi": "Confused log aatma ka aana, rehna ya jaana nahi dekhte. Samajh wale dekh lete hain."}, "15.11": {"en": "Dedicated yogis see the soul within themselves. Effort without a clear mind doesn't get you there.", "hi": "Dedicated yogi apne andar aatma dekhte hain. Bina saaf mind ke effort se nahi hota."}, "15.12": {"en": "The light of the sun, the moon and fire that lights up the world? That's me.", "hi": "Suraj, chaand aur aag ki roshni jo duniya ko roshan karti hai? Woh main hoon."}, "15.13": {"en": "I hold the earth together and support all life. I'm the nourishment in every plant.", "hi": "Main dharti ko sambhale hoon aur sab jeevan ko sahara deta hoon. Har paudhe ka poshan main hoon."}, "15.14": {"en": "I'm the fire of digestion inside you, working with your breath to process everything you eat.", "hi": "Main tumhare andar pachan ki aag hoon, saans ke saath mil ke jo khaate ho use pachata hoon."}, "15.15": {"en": "I'm in every heart. Memory, knowledge and forgetting come from me. Every scripture points to me.", "hi": "Main har dil mein hoon. Yaad, gyaan aur bhoolna mujhse aata hai. Har granth mujhe hi batata hai."}, "15.16": {"en": "There are two kinds of beings: those that perish and the one that doesn't.", "hi": "Do tarah ke jeev hain: jo nasht hote hain aur jo nahi hota."}, "15.17": {"en": "Beyond both is the Supreme Self, who enters and sustains all three worlds.", "hi": "Dono se pare param aatma hai, jo teenon lokon mein samaa ke unhe sambhalta hai."}, "15.18": {"en": "I'm beyond the perishable and higher than the imperishable. That's why I'm called the Supreme Person.", "hi": "Main nashwar se pare aur anashwar se bhi ooncha hoon. Isliye mujhe Purushottam kehte hain."}, "15.19": {"en": "Whoever knows me this way, without confusion, knows everything and loves me fully.", "hi": "Jo mujhe aise, bina confusion jaanta hai, woh sab jaanta hai aur mujhe poori tarah pyaar karta hai."}, "15.20": {"en": "That's the deepest secret. Understand it and you're truly wise, and your life's work is done.", "hi": "Yahi sabse gehra raaz hai. Ise samjho toh tum sach mein gyaani ho, aur life ka kaam poora."}, "16.1": {"en": "Divine qualities: fearlessness, a clean heart, steady practice, generosity, self-control, study and honesty.", "hi": "Divya gun: nidarta, saaf dil, lagataar practice, daan, self-control, padhai aur imaandaari."}, "16.2": {"en": "Non-violence, truth, no anger, letting go, peace, no gossip, kindness to all, no greed, gentleness.", "hi": "Ahimsa, sach, gussa nahi, chhodna, shaanti, chugli nahi, sabpe daya, laalach nahi, narmi."}, "16.3": {"en": "Energy, forgiveness, courage, purity, no hate and no big ego. These are signs of a divine nature.", "hi": "Josh, kshama, himmat, shuddhta, nafrat nahi aur bada ego nahi. Ye divya nature ke sign hain."}, "16.4": {"en": "Showing off, arrogance, ego, anger, rudeness and ignorance are signs of a toxic nature.", "hi": "Dikhawa, ghamand, ego, gussa, badtameezi aur agyaan, ye toxic nature ke sign hain."}, "16.5": {"en": "Divine qualities set you free; toxic ones trap you. Relax, Arjuna, you've got the good kind.", "hi": "Divya gun free karte hain, toxic gun phansate hain. Relax Arjun, tumhare paas achhe wale hain."}, "16.6": {"en": "There are two types of people: divine and toxic. You've heard about the divine. Now the other side.", "hi": "Do tarah ke log hain: divya aur toxic. Divya ke baare mein sun liya. Ab dusra side."}, "16.7": {"en": "Toxic people don't know what to do or what to avoid. No integrity, no discipline, no truth.", "hi": "Toxic log nahi jaante kya karna hai, kya nahi. Na integrity, na discipline, na sach."}, "16.8": {"en": "They say: \"Nothing's real, there's no God, life is random and it's all about desire.\"", "hi": "Woh kehte hain: \"Kuch real nahi, Bhagwan nahi, life random hai aur sab bas chahat ke liye hai.\""}, "16.9": {"en": "With that mindset they lose themselves and do harmful things that damage the world.", "hi": "Is soch se woh khud ko kho dete hain aur aise kaam karte hain jo duniya ko nuksaan pahunchate hain."}, "16.10": {"en": "Endless desires, shady money, ego and showing off. That's how they live.", "hi": "Kabhi na khatam hone wali chahatein, galat paisa, ego aur dikhawa. Aise jeete hain."}, "16.11": {"en": "They worry endlessly until death, and believe pleasure is the only point of life.", "hi": "Woh maut tak bina ruke chinta karte hain, aur maante hain ki maza hi life ka point hai."}, "16.12": {"en": "Trapped by a hundred hopes, ruled by desire and anger, they grab money any way they can.", "hi": "Sau umeedon mein phanse, chahat aur gusse ke ghulaam, kisi bhi tarah paisa jodte hain."}, "16.13": {"en": "\"I got this today, I'll get that tomorrow. This is mine, and that'll be mine too.\" Never enough.", "hi": "\"Aaj ye mila, kal woh milega. Ye mera hai, woh bhi mera hoga.\" Kabhi kaafi nahi."}, "16.14": {"en": "\"I destroyed that rival, I'll take down the rest. I'm the boss, I'm winning, I'm powerful.\"", "hi": "\"Us rival ko khatam kiya, baakiyon ko bhi karunga. Main boss hoon, main jeet raha hoon, main powerful hoon.\""}, "16.15": {"en": "\"I'm rich and well-connected. Who's like me? I'll donate and party.\" Clout chasing, ancient edition.", "hi": "\"Main ameer hoon, connections wala. Mere jaisa kaun? Daan karunga, party karunga.\" Clout chasing, purana version."}, "16.16": {"en": "Lost in a hundred thoughts, stuck in a web of illusion, hooked on pleasure, they fall hard.", "hi": "Sau khayalon mein khoye, maya ke jaal mein phanse, mazon ke addict, woh buri tarah girte hain."}, "16.17": {"en": "Full of themselves and drunk on money and pride, they do good deeds only for show.", "hi": "Apne aap mein mast, paise aur ghamand ke nashe mein, achhe kaam bhi sirf dikhawe ke liye karte hain."}, "16.18": {"en": "Driven by ego, power, pride, lust and anger, they end up hating the divine in themselves and others.", "hi": "Ego, power, ghamand, vaasna aur gusse se chal ke, woh apne aur dusron ke andar ke divine se nafrat karte hain."}, "16.19": {"en": "Cruel, hateful people keep getting pulled back into toxic cycles. What you give, you get.", "hi": "Kroor, nafrat bhare log baar-baar toxic cycles mein kheeche jaate hain. Jo doge, wahi paoge."}, "16.20": {"en": "Life after life they sink lower, never reaching me.", "hi": "Janam dar janam woh aur neeche girte hain, mujh tak kabhi nahi pahunchte."}, "16.21": {"en": "Lust, anger and greed: the three doors to self-destruction. Close all three.", "hi": "Vaasna, gussa aur laalach: khud ko barbaad karne ke teen darwaaze. Teeno band karo."}, "16.22": {"en": "Escape those three and you start working for your own real good, and you reach the highest.", "hi": "In teeno se bacho toh apne asli bhale ke liye kaam karte ho, aur sabse ooncha paate ho."}, "16.23": {"en": "Ignore all guidance and just follow your cravings? You get no success, no happiness and no freedom.", "hi": "Saari guidance ignore karke bas cravings follow karo? Na success, na khushi, na freedom."}, "16.24": {"en": "So let wisdom be your guide on what to do and what not to do, and then act.", "hi": "Toh kya karna hai aur kya nahi, ismein gyaan ko apna guide banao, phir kaam karo."}, "17.1": {"en": "Arjuna: \"What about people who skip the rules but still have faith? What kind of faith is that?\"", "hi": "Arjun: \"Jo rules skip karte hain par bharosa rakhte hain? Woh kaisa bharosa hai?\""}, "17.2": {"en": "Krishna: \"Faith comes in three types, based on your nature: pure, passionate or dark.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Bharosa teen tarah ka hota hai, tumhari nature ke hisaab se: shuddh, josh bhara ya andhera.\""}, "17.3": {"en": "You are what you believe in. Your faith shapes who you become.", "hi": "Tum wahi ho jis pe tum bharosa karte ho. Tumhara vishwas tay karta hai tum kya bante ho."}, "17.4": {"en": "Pure people worship the divine, passionate people chase power, dark-minded people worship ghosts and spirits.", "hi": "Shuddh log divine ko poojte hain, josh wale power ke peeche, andhere wale bhoot-pret ko poojte hain."}, "17.5": {"en": "Some people do extreme self-punishment just to show off, driven by ego and desire.", "hi": "Kuch log sirf dikhane ke liye extreme tapasya karte hain, ego aur chahat se chal ke."}, "17.6": {"en": "Hurting your own body isn't spiritual. It hurts the divine in you too. That's a toxic mindset.", "hi": "Apne body ko takleef dena spiritual nahi. Isse tumhare andar ka divine bhi hurt hota hai. Ye toxic mindset hai."}, "17.7": {"en": "Even food comes in three types. So does worship, discipline and giving. Let's break it down.", "hi": "Khaana bhi teen tarah ka hota hai. Pooja, tapasya aur daan bhi. Chalo breakdown karte hain."}, "17.8": {"en": "Pure food: fresh, nourishing, wholesome, satisfying. It boosts health, energy, focus and happiness.", "hi": "Shuddh khaana: taaza, poshak, healthy, santusht karne wala. Sehat, energy, focus aur khushi badhata hai."}, "17.9": {"en": "Passionate food: too spicy, salty, sour or hot. Tastes intense, leaves you uncomfortable and unwell.", "hi": "Rajasi khaana: zyada teekha, namkeen, khatta ya garam. Swaad intense, baad mein takleef aur bimaari."}, "17.10": {"en": "Dark food: stale, leftover, tasteless, rotten. Junk that drags you down.", "hi": "Tamasi khaana: baasi, bacha hua, bina swaad, sada hua. Junk jo tumhe neeche kheenchta hai."}, "17.11": {"en": "Pure worship is done because it's right, without expecting anything back.", "hi": "Shuddh pooja isliye hoti hai kyunki sahi hai, bina kuch wapas chahe."}, "17.12": {"en": "Worship done for rewards or to show off is the passionate kind.", "hi": "Reward ke liye ya dikhawe ke liye ki gayi pooja rajasi hai."}, "17.13": {"en": "Worship with no faith, no care, no sincerity and no giving is the dark kind.", "hi": "Bina bharose, bina parwaah, bina sachchai aur bina daan ki pooja tamasi hai."}, "17.14": {"en": "Discipline of the body: respecting teachers and elders, staying clean, honest, self-controlled and non-violent.", "hi": "Body ka tap: guru aur badon ki izzat, saaf rehna, imaandaari, self-control aur ahimsa."}, "17.15": {"en": "Discipline of speech: saying what's true, kind and helpful, without hurting anyone.", "hi": "Vaani ka tap: jo sach, pyaara aur faydemand ho woh bolna, bina kisi ko hurt kiye."}, "17.16": {"en": "Discipline of the mind: calm, kind, quiet, self-controlled and pure thoughts.", "hi": "Mann ka tap: shaant, dayalu, maun, self-controlled aur shuddh vichaar."}, "17.17": {"en": "All three done with faith and no expectations? That's the purest discipline.", "hi": "Teeno bharose aur bina umeed ke kiye? Ye sabse shuddh tap hai."}, "17.18": {"en": "Discipline done for likes, respect and praise is the passionate kind. It doesn't last.", "hi": "Likes, izzat aur taareef ke liye kiya tap rajasi hai. Ye tikta nahi."}, "17.19": {"en": "Discipline that's self-torture or meant to harm others is the dark kind.", "hi": "Jo tap khud ko takleef dene ya dusron ko nuksaan ke liye ho, woh tamasi hai."}, "17.20": {"en": "Giving because it's right, to someone who deserves it, at the right time, expecting nothing back. That's pure giving.", "hi": "Sahi samajh ke dena, sahi insaan ko, sahi time pe, bina kuch wapas chahe. Ye shuddh daan hai."}, "17.21": {"en": "Giving to get something back, or giving reluctantly, is the passionate kind.", "hi": "Kuch wapas paane ke liye dena, ya bemann se dena, rajasi daan hai."}, "17.22": {"en": "Giving at the wrong time, to the wrong person, with disrespect, is the dark kind.", "hi": "Galat time pe, galat insaan ko, bina izzat ke dena tamasi daan hai."}, "17.23": {"en": "\"Om Tat Sat\": three sacred words that point to the ultimate truth.", "hi": "\"Om Tat Sat\": teen pavitra shabd jo param satya ki taraf ishaara karte hain."}, "17.24": {"en": "That's why the wise begin every sacred act by saying \"Om\".", "hi": "Isliye gyaani har pavitra kaam \"Om\" bol ke shuru karte hain."}, "17.25": {"en": "Seekers say \"Tat\" and act without wanting rewards. It means: this is for the divine, not me.", "hi": "Saadhak \"Tat\" bol ke bina reward chahe kaam karte hain. Matlab: ye divine ke liye hai, mere liye nahi."}, "17.26": {"en": "\"Sat\" means truth and goodness. Any good deed is called Sat.", "hi": "\"Sat\" ka matlab sach aur achhai. Har achha kaam Sat kehlata hai."}, "17.27": {"en": "Staying committed to worship, discipline and giving is Sat too. So is any work done for that purpose.", "hi": "Pooja, tap aur daan mein lage rehna bhi Sat hai. Us maksad se kiya har kaam bhi."}, "17.28": {"en": "Anything done without faith, even if it looks spiritual, is empty. Faith is what makes it count.", "hi": "Bina bharose kiya kuch bhi, chahe spiritual dikhe, khaali hai. Bharosa hi use count karata hai."}, "18.1": {"en": "Arjuna: \"What's the real difference between renouncing and letting go?\" The final chapter begins.", "hi": "Arjun: \"Sanyas aur tyaag mein asli farak kya hai?\" Aakhri chapter shuru."}, "18.2": {"en": "Renouncing means dropping selfish actions. Letting go means doing your work but dropping the attachment to results.", "hi": "Sanyas matlab selfish kaam chhodna. Tyaag matlab kaam karna par result ka attachment chhodna."}, "18.3": {"en": "Some say quit all action. Others say keep doing good things like charity and discipline.", "hi": "Kuch kehte hain sab karm chhodo. Kuch kehte hain daan aur tap jaise achhe kaam karte raho."}, "18.4": {"en": "Krishna: \"Here's my final take. Letting go comes in three types.\"", "hi": "Krishna: \"Ye mera final verdict hai. Tyaag teen tarah ka hota hai.\""}, "18.5": {"en": "Worship, charity and discipline shouldn't be dropped. They purify even wise people.", "hi": "Pooja, daan aur tap chhodne nahi chahiye. Ye gyaaniyon ko bhi shuddh karte hain."}, "18.6": {"en": "But even these should be done without attachment or expecting results. That's my final answer.", "hi": "Par ye bhi bina attachment aur bina result ki umeed ke karne chahiye. Ye mera final answer hai."}, "18.7": {"en": "Ditching your duties out of confusion? That's the lazy, dark kind of quitting.", "hi": "Confusion mein apni duty chhod dena? Ye aalsi, andhere wala tyaag hai."}, "18.8": {"en": "Quitting because something's hard or uncomfortable? That's the restless kind, and it gets you nothing.", "hi": "Kuch mushkil ya uncomfortable hai isliye chhodna? Ye bechain tyaag hai, aur isse kuch nahi milta."}, "18.9": {"en": "Doing your duty fully while letting go of attachment and results? That's the pure kind.", "hi": "Apni duty poori karna, par attachment aur result chhod ke? Ye shuddh tyaag hai."}, "18.10": {"en": "A truly wise person doesn't avoid unpleasant work or cling to pleasant work. No doubts, just clarity.", "hi": "Sachcha gyaani na bura kaam avoid karta hai, na achhe se chipakta hai. Doubt nahi, bas clarity."}, "18.11": {"en": "You can't stop acting while you have a body. Real letting go means letting go of results.", "hi": "Jab tak body hai, karm rok nahi sakte. Asli tyaag matlab result chhodna."}, "18.12": {"en": "If you cling to results, you get good, bad or mixed karma. Let go and none of it sticks.", "hi": "Result se chipko toh achha, bura ya mixed karma milta hai. Chhod do toh kuch nahi chipakta."}, "18.13": {"en": "Every action has five causes. Let me break them down.", "hi": "Har karm ke paanch kaaran hote hain. Chalo breakdown karta hoon."}, "18.14": {"en": "The body, the doer, the senses, the various efforts, and divine will. Five factors behind every action.", "hi": "Body, karne wala, senses, alag-alag koshishein, aur divine ichchha. Har karm ke peeche paanch factors."}, "18.15": {"en": "Whatever you do with body, words or mind, right or wrong, these five are behind it.", "hi": "Body, shabd ya mann se jo bhi karo, sahi ya galat, ye paanch uske peeche hain."}, "18.16": {"en": "So thinking \"I alone did this\" is a limited view. You're only one of five factors.", "hi": "Toh sochna ki \"sab maine akele kiya\" chhoti soch hai. Tum paanch mein se bas ek factor ho."}, "18.17": {"en": "Someone with no \"I did it\" ego and a clean mind isn't bound by their actions.", "hi": "Jisme \"maine kiya\" wala ego nahi aur mann saaf hai, woh apne karm se bandhta nahi."}, "18.18": {"en": "Knowledge, the thing known and the knower drive action. The tool, the act and the doer make it happen.", "hi": "Gyaan, jaanne layak cheez aur jaanne wala karm ko chalate hain. Saadhan, kaam aur karta use poora karte hain."}, "18.19": {"en": "Knowledge, action and the doer each come in three types too. Here's how.", "hi": "Gyaan, karm aur karta bhi teen-teen tarah ke hote hain. Aise."}, "18.20": {"en": "Pure knowledge sees one unchanging reality in all beings. Unity in diversity.", "hi": "Shuddh gyaan sab jeevon mein ek hi atal sach dekhta hai. Anekta mein ekta."}, "18.21": {"en": "Passionate knowledge sees everyone as totally separate and different. Us versus them.", "hi": "Rajasi gyaan sabko bilkul alag-alag dekhta hai. Hum versus woh."}, "18.22": {"en": "Dark knowledge fixates on one small thing as if it's everything. Narrow, illogical, shallow.", "hi": "Tamasi gyaan ek chhoti cheez ko hi sab kuch maan leta hai. Tang, bina tark, khokhla."}, "18.23": {"en": "Pure action: doing what's needed, without attachment, likes or dislikes, or wanting rewards.", "hi": "Shuddh karm: jo zaroori hai woh karna, bina attachment, pasand-naapasand ya reward ki chahat."}, "18.24": {"en": "Passionate action: lots of stress and effort, all to satisfy your ego and desires.", "hi": "Rajasi karm: bahut stress aur mehnat, sab ego aur chahat poori karne ke liye."}, "18.25": {"en": "Dark action: done blindly, ignoring consequences, harm to others, and your own limits.", "hi": "Tamasi karm: andhadhundh, nateeje, dusron ka nuksaan aur apni limits ignore karke."}, "18.26": {"en": "A pure doer: no attachment, no bragging, steady, enthusiastic, unbothered by success or failure.", "hi": "Shuddh karta: na attachment, na shekhi, steady, utsaahi, success ya failure se unbothered."}, "18.27": {"en": "A passionate doer: attached, result-obsessed, greedy, harmful, and on an emotional rollercoaster.", "hi": "Rajasi karta: attached, result ka obsessed, laalchi, nuksaandeh, aur emotional rollercoaster pe."}, "18.28": {"en": "A dark doer: careless, stubborn, dishonest, lazy, gloomy and always procrastinating.", "hi": "Tamasi karta: laparwah, ziddi, beimaan, aalsi, udaas aur hamesha taalne wala."}, "18.29": {"en": "Now the three types of intellect and willpower.", "hi": "Ab buddhi aur dhairya ke teen prakaar."}, "18.30": {"en": "Pure intellect knows what to do and avoid, when to fear and when not, what binds and what frees.", "hi": "Shuddh buddhi jaanti hai kya karna aur kya nahi, kab darna aur kab nahi, kya baandhta aur kya free karta."}, "18.31": {"en": "Passionate intellect gets confused between right and wrong, what to do and what not to do.", "hi": "Rajasi buddhi sahi-galat, karna-na karna mein confuse ho jaati hai."}, "18.32": {"en": "Dark intellect sees wrong as right and flips every value upside down.", "hi": "Tamasi buddhi galat ko sahi dekhti hai aur har value ulti kar deti hai."}, "18.33": {"en": "Pure willpower keeps your mind, breath and senses steady through practice. Unshakeable focus.", "hi": "Shuddh dhairya practice se mind, saans aur senses steady rakhta hai. Atal focus."}, "18.34": {"en": "Passionate willpower holds tight to duty, desire and wealth, but only for what you'll get out of it.", "hi": "Rajasi dhairya duty, chahat aur paise ko pakad ke rakhta hai, par sirf apne fayde ke liye."}, "18.35": {"en": "Dark willpower is just being stubborn about not giving up sleep, fear, sadness and ego.", "hi": "Tamasi dhairya bas neend, darr, udaasi aur ego na chhodne ki zid hai."}, "18.36": {"en": "Now the three kinds of happiness. Real joy builds with practice and ends your pain.", "hi": "Ab khushi ke teen prakaar. Asli khushi practice se banti hai aur dukh khatam karti hai."}, "18.37": {"en": "Pure happiness feels like medicine at first but becomes nectar. It comes from a calm, clear mind.", "hi": "Shuddh khushi pehle dawai jaisi kadwi lagti hai par baad mein amrit. Shaant, saaf mann se aati hai."}, "18.38": {"en": "Passionate happiness feels like nectar at first but turns into poison. Instant gratification, long-term regret.", "hi": "Rajasi khushi pehle amrit jaisi lagti hai par baad mein zehar. Instant maza, baad mein pachhtava."}, "18.39": {"en": "Dark happiness comes from oversleeping, laziness and carelessness. It fools you from start to finish.", "hi": "Tamasi khushi zyada neend, aalas aur laparwahi se aati hai. Shuru se ant tak dhokha deti hai."}, "18.40": {"en": "No one, on earth or in heaven, is free from these three energies.", "hi": "Dharti ya swarg mein koi bhi in teen energies se free nahi hai."}, "18.41": {"en": "People's roles in society are meant to match their natural qualities, not their birth.", "hi": "Samaaj mein logon ka role unki natural qualities se match hona chahiye, janam se nahi."}, "18.42": {"en": "Thinkers and teachers by nature: calm, disciplined, pure, patient, honest, wise and full of faith.", "hi": "Nature se sochne aur sikhane wale: shaant, disciplined, shuddh, sabr wale, imaandaar, gyaani aur bharose wale."}, "18.43": {"en": "Leaders and protectors by nature: brave, energetic, steady, skilled, generous and never running from a fight.", "hi": "Nature se leader aur rakshak: bahadur, energetic, steady, skilled, daani aur ladai se kabhi na bhaagne wale."}, "18.44": {"en": "Builders, farmers and traders by nature create wealth. Those who love serving keep everything running.", "hi": "Nature se banane wale, kisaan aur vyapaari daulat banate hain. Seva pasand log sab chalate rehte hain."}, "18.45": {"en": "Dedicate yourself to your own natural work and you reach perfection. Here's how.", "hi": "Apne natural kaam mein dil lagao aur perfection tak pahunchoge. Aise."}, "18.46": {"en": "Do your own work as worship of the one who created everything, and you'll reach perfection.", "hi": "Apna kaam us rachnakar ki pooja samajh ke karo jisne sab banaya, aur perfection paoge."}, "18.47": {"en": "Your own path done imperfectly beats someone else's done perfectly. Doing your own thing keeps you clean.", "hi": "Apna raasta imperfect bhi better hai kisi aur ke perfect se. Apna kaam karna tumhe saaf rakhta hai."}, "18.48": {"en": "Don't quit your work just because it's imperfect. Every effort has some flaw, like fire has smoke.", "hi": "Kaam imperfect hai isliye mat chhodo. Har koshish mein kuch kami hoti hai, jaise aag mein dhuaan."}, "18.49": {"en": "Unattached, self-controlled, free from craving. Through letting go, you reach the ultimate freedom.", "hi": "Bina attachment, self-controlled, craving se free. Chhodne se tum param freedom paate ho."}, "18.50": {"en": "Here's the short version of how a perfected person reaches the ultimate.", "hi": "Ye raha short version ki perfect insaan ultimate tak kaise pahunchta hai."}, "18.51": {"en": "A clear mind, steady self-control, stepping back from distractions, and dropping love-hate drama.", "hi": "Saaf mann, steady self-control, distractions se door, aur pasand-naapasand ka drama khatam."}, "18.52": {"en": "Enjoying solitude, eating light, controlling body, speech and mind, meditating, staying detached.", "hi": "Akelapan enjoy karna, halka khaana, body, vaani aur mann pe control, dhyaan, detached rehna."}, "18.53": {"en": "Dropping ego, power trips, pride, lust, anger and hoarding. No \"mine\". Total peace.", "hi": "Ego, power trips, ghamand, vaasna, gussa aur jama karna chhodna. \"Mera\" kuch nahi. Poori shaanti."}, "18.54": {"en": "At peace, without grief or craving, seeing everyone as equal, you find the highest love for me.", "hi": "Shaant, na dukh na craving, sabko barabar dekhte hue, tum mere liye sabse ooncha pyaar paate ho."}, "18.55": {"en": "Through that love you truly know who I am. And knowing me, you become one with me.", "hi": "Us pyaar se tum sach mein jaante ho main kaun hoon. Aur mujhe jaan ke mujhse ek ho jaate ho."}, "18.56": {"en": "Keep doing your work while trusting me, and by my grace you reach the eternal home.", "hi": "Mujh pe bharosa rakh ke kaam karte raho, aur meri kripa se amar ghar paoge."}, "18.57": {"en": "Mentally hand over all your actions to me, make me your goal, and keep your thoughts on me.", "hi": "Mann se apne saare karm mujhe saunp do, mujhe goal banao, aur khayal mujh pe rakho."}, "18.58": {"en": "Keep me in mind and you'll get through every obstacle. Ignore me out of ego and you'll struggle.", "hi": "Mujhe yaad rakho toh har mushkil paar karoge. Ego mein ignore karoge toh struggle karoge."}, "18.59": {"en": "\"I won't fight\"? Your ego is talking. Your own nature will push you to act anyway.", "hi": "\"Main nahi ladunga\"? Ye tumhara ego bol raha hai. Tumhari nature tumse karwa hi legi."}, "18.60": {"en": "What you refuse to do out of confusion, your nature will make you do anyway.", "hi": "Jo confusion mein karne se mana kar rahe ho, tumhari nature waise bhi karwa degi."}, "18.61": {"en": "The divine lives in every heart and moves all beings, like riders on a wheel.", "hi": "Divine har dil mein rehta hai aur sab jeevon ko chalata hai, jaise chakkar pe baithe log."}, "18.62": {"en": "Turn to the divine with everything you've got. By that grace you'll find supreme peace.", "hi": "Poori jaan se divine ki sharan lo. Us kripa se param shaanti milegi."}, "18.63": {"en": "That's the deepest wisdom. Think it through fully, then do what you choose. Your call.", "hi": "Ye sabse gehra gyaan hai. Poora soch lo, phir jo chaho karo. Tumhari choice."}, "18.64": {"en": "\"Listen to my most secret message once more. I'm telling you because I care about you deeply.\"", "hi": "\"Mera sabse secret message ek baar aur suno. Bata raha hoon kyunki tumhari bahut parwaah hai.\""}, "18.65": {"en": "Keep your mind on me, love me, honour me, bow to me. You'll come to me. That's my promise.", "hi": "Mind mujh pe rakho, pyaar karo, izzat do, jhuko. Mere paas aaoge. Ye mera vaada hai."}, "18.66": {"en": "Drop the pressure and overthinking. Trust me completely and I've got you. Don't stress.", "hi": "Saara pressure aur overthinking chhodo. Mujh par poora bharosa rakho, main hoon na. Tension mat lo."}, "18.67": {"en": "Don't force this on people who aren't interested, aren't disciplined, or mock it.", "hi": "Ye un logon pe mat thopo jo interested nahi, disciplined nahi, ya mazaak udaate hain."}, "18.68": {"en": "Whoever shares this wisdom with sincere seekers will surely come to me.", "hi": "Jo ye gyaan sachche seekers ke saath share karega, woh zaroor mere paas aayega."}, "18.69": {"en": "No one does anything dearer to me than that. Nobody will be dearer to me.", "hi": "Isse zyada pyaara kaam mere liye koi nahi karta. Koi mujhe isse zyada pyaara nahi hoga."}, "18.70": {"en": "Even studying this conversation counts as worshipping me through knowledge.", "hi": "Is baat-cheet ko padhna bhi gyaan se meri pooja maana jaayega."}, "18.71": {"en": "And just listening with faith, without picking holes, sets you free too.", "hi": "Aur bas bharose se sunna, bina nukta-cheeni ke, bhi tumhe free karta hai."}, "18.72": {"en": "\"Arjuna, did you really listen? Is your confusion gone?\" The ultimate check-in.", "hi": "\"Arjun, kya tumne sach mein suna? Confusion gaya?\" Ultimate check-in."}, "18.73": {"en": "Arjuna: \"My confusion is gone. I remember who I am. No doubts left. I'll do what you say.\" Glow-up complete.", "hi": "Arjun: \"Mera confusion chala gaya. Mujhe yaad aa gaya main kaun hoon. Koi doubt nahi. Jo aap kahoge karunga.\" Glow-up complete."}, "18.74": {"en": "Sanjaya: \"I heard this amazing conversation between Krishna and Arjuna. Goosebumps.\"", "hi": "Sanjay: \"Maine Krishna aur Arjun ki ye adbhut baat suni. Rongte khade ho gaye.\""}, "18.75": {"en": "\"Thanks to Vyasa, I heard this highest wisdom straight from Krishna himself.\"", "hi": "\"Vyas ji ki kripa se maine ye param gyaan seedha Krishna se suna.\""}, "18.76": {"en": "\"Every time I remember this conversation, I feel joy all over again.\"", "hi": "\"Jab bhi ye baat-cheet yaad aati hai, phir se khushi hoti hai.\""}, "18.77": {"en": "\"And remembering that cosmic form of Krishna, I'm amazed again and again.\"", "hi": "\"Aur Krishna ka woh vishwaroop yaad karke baar-baar hairaan hota hoon.\""}, "18.78": {"en": "Wherever Krishna's wisdom and Arjuna's action meet, there's success, prosperity and doing what's right. Final word.", "hi": "Jahan Krishna ka gyaan aur Arjun ka karm milte hain, wahan jeet, samriddhi aur dharm hota hai. Aakhri baat."}};
